{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution","id":808930,"title":"Improving the Standard of Living without recreating the Industrial Revolution","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-14T12:17:14-08:00","id":808930,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Improving the Standard of Living without recreating the Industrial Revolution","content":"Hey, I have an idea of a Twilight Crafter that wants to improve the living conditions of Creation for mortals. Any ideas how I can do that without recreating the Industrial Revolution or the Ex2 First Age?<br /> <br /> Here are some areas of improvement areas I thought of:<br /> <br /> Clean Water<br /> Abundant Food<br /> Climate Control<br /> Health Care<br /> Safe Lighting<br /> Faster Travel<br /> Better Communication<br /> More Accessible Education<br /> Better Safety/Law Enforcement<br /> <br /> One idea I had was focusing on the community instead of the individual. For example, instead of everyone having a phone, you go to the phone office or something like that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":".  Added another idea 01-14-2016, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:22:43-08:00","id":808938,"title":"","content":"Tools. Especially ones that make other tools. Engineering principles and tradecraft, generally.<br /> <br /> These are big ones for my game's Twilight. Proper toolmaking allows communities to derive radically better returns on their inputs of human labor, and practical engineering knowledge puts these communities in a far better position to achieve both safety and prosperity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:36:47-08:00","id":808955,"title":"","content":"You mentioned it already, but...health and sanitation. Like <i>holy crap this</i>. Quality of life and productivity go way up when people don't have to worry about contagion all the time. If I were a god-touched miracle worker who wanted to improve the living conditions of people on a large scale, the first thing I'd do is start drawing up civil engineering plans for aqueducts and sewage disposal systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:38:39-08:00","id":808957,"title":"","content":"You can dig wells for people. Maybe introduce irrigation canals or help them improve their farming.<br /> <br /> Seriously, playing a Twilight <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norman_Borlaug\" target=\"_blank\">Norman Borlaug</a> would be awesome IMO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=808955#post808955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mentioned it already, but...health and sanitation. Like <i>holy crap this</i>. Quality of life and productivity go way up when people don't have to worry about contagion all the time. If I were a god-touched miracle worker who wanted to improve the living conditions of people on a large scale, the first thing I'd do is start drawing up civil engineering plans for aqueducts and sewage disposal systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>This too. Introducing ideas such as &quot;Hey, what if we DON'T just throw our shit into the streets?&quot; and &quot;Maybe we should wash our hands once a day&quot; could be <b>massive</b>. Like how <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ignaz_Semmelweis\" target=\"_blank\">Ignaz Semmelweis</a> noticed that if you washed and disinfected your hands before a surgery, the patient's chances of survival increased drastically. Just small ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 01-14-2016, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:42:55-08:00","id":808962,"title":"","content":"The key to economic growth and diversification is a surplus of food. If you can use a relatively small number of people to grow enough food for a relatively large number of people, that makes enough idle hands that skill specialization is the logical choice.<br /> <br /> To that end, I would focus on projects that promote farm productivity and ease trade, such as dams, irrigation ditches/canals, roads, etc. Once you have a critical mass of &quot;idle&quot; labor in cities or larger townships, you have a solid foundation.<br /> <br /> The next step is to develop your trades. You create policies that reward trade guilds and professionals. Make a point of recruiting excellent smiths, architects, doctors, etc, and give them land/titles, and incentivize them to teach, rather than produce. Being a Solar, you can afford to wait a few decades for this to pay off.<br /> <br /> Once you have a really solid agricultural and artisan economy, then you leverage that wealth to bankroll an education system. I would start with a focused public education that does just the basics (math, writing), because that will feed back into your artisan class. Then create a &quot;higher&quot; education system, and recruit the best minds to do it (or train them yourself; you're a Twilight.).Make that also public and free, but competitive. This gets you the best minds from your citizens as your &quot;white collar&quot; bureaucrats, project managers, etc.<br /> <br /> The best way to avoid the &quot;Industrial&quot; effect is to just not head in the direction of mass-production, and agree with your ST that's not what you want for the game. Your nation's culture emphasizes art, reliability, and craftsmanship over low prices and high volume.<br /> <br /> Once you're at stage three, so to speak, you have a model that can easily be replicated elsewhere. Just transplant some of your young journeyman and &quot;college&quot; graduates to new territory, and repeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","user":"Totentanz","date":".  Typo 01-14-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:43:38-08:00","id":808963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=808957#post808957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can dig wells for people. Maybe introduce irrigation canals or help them improve their farming.<br /> <br /> Seriously, playing a Twilight <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norman_Borlaug\" target=\"_blank\">Norman Borlaug</a> would be awesome IMO.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This too. Introducing ideas such as &quot;Hey, what if we DON'T just throw our shit into the streets?&quot; and &quot;Maybe we should wash our hands once a day&quot; could be <b>massive</b>. Like how <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ignaz_Semmelweis\" target=\"_blank\">Ignaz Semmelweis</a> noticed that if you washed and disinfected your hands before a surgery, the patient's chances of survival increased drastically. Just small ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm... Would Linguistics or Socialize be better for superpowering a hand washing campaign? I don't know the Ex3 charms that well yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:44:11-08:00","id":808965,"title":"","content":"Clean water is pretty easy actually. If the water is dirty, summon up some water cleaner elementals to clean the water for you. In Nexus's case you may want several dozen. If the God of Pollution or small gods of dirty water show up, kill them.<br /> <br /> Abundant Food = Survival charms. I remember reading homebrew charms a while back of Survival charms that greatly increased yield of crops. Survival needs a bone other than animal and environmental protection, so this seems fine.<br /> <br /> Climate control = Workings or very lavish bribes to weather gods. If they start to get uppity, have a backup plan to make their lives hell.<br /> <br /> Safe Lighting is from the glowstones of Gem.<br /> <br /> Faster Travel is something that is problematic. Charms can help solve this, as does being a Sorcerer. I can't think of any other way.<br /> <br /> Better communication is iffy as hell. There is already &quot;God Prayer relay&quot; system mentioned in 1e Cult of the Illuminated, which I actually enjoyed. Sorcerous magical mirrors or that one skull talking necromancy spell helps.<br /> <br /> More Accessible Education can be done when basic need of survival are largely met. Even in the Nexus Philosopical schools one can audit courses by just attending them and listening. You won't be able to ask questions, but you can listen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:47:35-08:00","id":808969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=808955#post808955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mentioned it already, but...health and sanitation. Like <i>holy crap this</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was this a pun? I think it was a pun.<br /> <br /> Also: the way that living quarters and community spaces are architected have a <i>staggeringly, ridiculously </i>enormous effect on the quality and nature of the social interactions carried out within them. Spending effort designing and building living arrangements that ensured easy access to quality sanitation, socialization/family needs, and privacy would be another good way to make large quality of life improvements.<br /> <br /> Also, another thing I just thought of: building using effective natural materials. You can build effective structures out of way more kinds of materials than most folks would suspect, and clever materials choices can seriously mitigate the need for climate control in an enormous variety of climates and biomes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","user":"Zeesun","date":". 01-14-2016, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:56:48-08:00","id":808980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=808955#post808955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the first thing I'd do is start drawing up civil engineering plans for aqueducts and sewage disposal systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go big, or go home! Sorcerous Working that makes the villagers 100% energy efficient and evolve past the biological need for butts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:01:54-08:00","id":808990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=808965#post808965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faster Travel is something that is problematic. Charms can help solve this, as does being a Sorcerer. I can't think of any other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to think of another way. The Romans already did it for you. Well-maintained, safe roads will do more for the masses of people than any Charm will. If you happen to be a sorcerer then sure, Workings can help this, but I've already noticed a tendency among some people to point toward Workings as the go-to solution to any problem and I'd like to push back against that a little. You don't need to go straight to sorcery to revolutionize travel. Paving stones and good relations with your local road deities will do that pretty well.<br /> <br /> This is a little bit of a side-topic, but I actually have a pet theory that a big part of the once-every-two-years Guild Councils in Nexus revolve around negotiating large scale standing contracts with directional travel gods guaranteeing safe, timely passage of Guild caravans along major trade routes. The Guild then licenses regional trade consortiums at a hefty fee, allowing them to benefit from those pacts and giving them an enormous advantage over unlicensed traders, who don't get the protections and assistance of the signatory spirit courts. The regional trade groups abide by set business practices dictated by the Council but are otherwise self-governing. The Guild itself acts sort of like a multinational corporate conglomerate with enormous resources and leverage because of its vast reach, but when you get right down to it the guys at the top don't actually run most stuff. They franchise out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:03:25-08:00","id":808991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=808963#post808963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... Would Linguistics or Socialize be better for superpowering a hand washing campaign? I don't know the Ex3 charms that well yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, odd. I vaguely recall a Charm idea that was teased way back before the release that there was a Socialize Charm that could let you make blanket changes to a culture's behavior. Like &quot;Everyone must bathe daily&quot;. But I can't seem to find it now.<br /> <br /> Anyway... Socialize would probably be better. Or Bureaucracy. Linguistics is more for written things, and you'd probably be working with outlying territories that probably won't be especially literate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:23:58-08:00","id":809020,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure your exalt would be successful in raising living conditions by making manga to encourage reading for the young folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:25:16-08:00","id":809023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809020#post809020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure your exalt would be successful in raising living conditions by making manga to encourage reading for the young folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shh... This is a different character for a different project. :P <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:37:23-08:00","id":809039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=808991#post808991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, odd. I vaguely recall a Charm idea that was teased way back before the release that there was a Socialize Charm that could let you make blanket changes to a culture's behavior. Like &quot;Everyone must bathe daily&quot;. But I can't seem to find it now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe under Bureaucracy. It's a little restrictive, though. I guess it depends on how broadly you want to read the term &quot;organization&quot;. Still, if you can insist that all licensed physicians in the city have to wash their hands regularly, that would probably go a long way toward the goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:00:15-08:00","id":809063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can use a relatively small number of people to grow enough food for a relatively large number of people, that makes enough idle hands that skill specialization is the logical choice.</div> </div> </div> </div> You can also get societies in which the relative ease of producing food and an abundance of available land means that everybody lives as a farmer, except with a really short working day, so there's a lot of leisure time. Even better is if you can add on some valuable livestock option on top of that, preferably one that breeds abundantly and requires very little upkeep. That's kind of what happened in England after the Black Death; reduced numbers of people meant large tracts of land and an emphasis on sheep farming (since it's really easy to raise sheep), and because of the high value of woll and good wages on account of a competitive labour pool, you had a lot of pretty affluent lower class people who didn't need to work very often. Reportedly, up to half the year could be spent in numerous festivities, often of that kind aimed at mocking the upper classes. Threatened aristocrats had to start bringing in sumptuary laws, because how are you supposed to tell class distinctions when everybody can afford at least one set of high-quality clothes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:11:20-08:00","id":809073,"title":"","content":"From the magic side of things, the way to avoid Dreams of the First Age is with a few very high level artifacts or workings doing a huge amount of heavy lifting each. Even effects with lots of small uses should all obviously come from the same thing.<br /> <br /> For example, instead of streetlights, central heating, and blast furnaces you build a giant red jade temple that makes on demand minor elementals for that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> What makes these schemes start to look technological is the ubiquity of individual pieces of technology. Giant gangs of slaves building a magic pyramid doesn't violate genre aesthetics even if that pyramid happens to also be wireless bank that teleports people's ritual money around. So you can get credit cards and wire fraud without looking too modern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:21:44-08:00","id":809084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809063#post809063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Threatened aristocrats had to start bringing in sumptuary laws, because how are you supposed to tell class distinctions when everybody can afford at least one set of high-quality clothes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god I haven't thought about sumptuary laws since my graduate seminars in Middle English. Thank you for this. I need to go read Bocaccio's <i>Decameron </i>again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:29:59-08:00","id":809095,"title":"","content":"That actually lends itself to an often unexamined concern of improving living standards, since you also need to overcome the prejudices of the authorities concerning whether people of a certain class and rank should even be allowed to have access to certain benefits and luxuries. It's no good building a thing if you're going to have people who are too powerful for you to merely ignore work dilligently to tear it down again. It's like the difference between giving a certain section of the population the right to vote and preventing local government from introducing all kinds of arbitrary restrictions on registering to exercise that right. Or, for a more contemporary example that relates directly to one of these subjects; you can make schools available, but also have to ensure that people won't be targeted for attacks if they attend them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:37:42-08:00","id":809102,"title":"","content":"Gonna need some social engineering to go along with your physical engineering if you want that Utopia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:43:24-08:00","id":809106,"title":"","content":"That's not a bad point, but at least for Solars, I think it's a surprisingly small problem in most cases.<br /> <br /> 3E works really hard to present Solars with the Superman problem - they can do almost anything, but can't be everywhere at once. All of their society-altering tricks, then, get balanced along ideas of scale - an even semi-focus Solar should be able to treat any disease/cross any distance/steal any object/persuade any person, but can only work on so many patients, only bring so many people on fast travel, etc. That's a compelling area to explore, and it does reintroduce many of the issues which were trivialized so quickly in 2E.<br /> <br /> But it also means that a Solar ruler is about a billion times better at getting a few dozen powerful people on board with her vision than she is at getting specific results from the general populace. In particular, any individual dissenter who (1) is known to the Solar and (2) lacks some MASSIVE supernatural protection can be swayed from a bitter enemy to a (literal) worshipful lackey in under half an hour. Adjusting the attitudes of the upper class as a whole is trickier, but ultimately doable (gather them together regularly for some impressive Performance recitals).<br /> <br /> Generally, where Solars are involved, the &quot;old aristocrats who impede your works not out of malice so much as scorn for the lessers you uplift&quot; seem less likely to be the upper class of whatever society you're working on, and more likely to be local gods, rival nations lacking a dialogue with you, and (of course) the Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:45:35-08:00","id":809110,"title":"","content":"I agree with the broad point, although I personally dislike the term &quot;social engineering&quot; because I associate it with high modernist disasters. I prefer to speak in terms of creating incentives; you create an incentive for a cash-based market economy in which the agrarian classes devote a lot of time to producing profitable goods by requiring them to pay taxes in cash. You attempt to engineer a city into being some uniform thing built according to a rigid grid plan in which there's a place for everything, and everything in its place (and then look in on bewilderment trying to figure out the inevitable failure on several fronts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:48:43-08:00","id":809113,"title":"","content":"You can use Performance to sway the masses, too. You just need to get them all together in one piece to hear your speech. So, add public amphitheaters and a yearly festival to hear the Great Leader speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:50:04-08:00","id":809116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809110#post809110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with the broad point, although I personally dislike the term &quot;social engineering&quot; because I associate it with high modernist disasters.</div> </div> </div> </div>My tongue was lodged <i>firmly </i>in my check when I wrote that sentence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T15:04:33-08:00","id":809128,"title":"","content":"Any talk of using Solar Charms to influence society at large should keep in mind how dependent so many things are on the general social system now. People are not mere puppets to the first Solar who speaks to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T15:12:09-08:00","id":809135,"title":"","content":"Do stuff that technology can't do.<br /> <br /> -Get disease gods to shrink their own domains in exchange for prayer.<br /> <br /> -Make all the animals in the land friendly.<br /> <br /> -Put the weather on a schedule, and forbid hurricanes from coming anywhere near cities.<br /> <br /> -Bless the earth so that it brings forth food without labour.<br /> <br /> -Teach minor magic to every mortal, so that anyone who gets a headache can banish it with an incantation.<br /> <br /> -Be so ridiculously charismatic and beautiful that everyone who sees you is filled with joy and a desire to do good works.<br /> <br /> -Run the government so efficiently that there's no such thing as corruption and all the paperwork is simple.<br /> <br /> -Write a book that ends slavery, by telling the story of a slave so touchingly that anyone who reads it becomes horrified by the institution.<br /> <br /> -Solve major crimes so reliably that people stop committing them.<br /> <br /> -Stab any tyrant who gets too tyrannical, after making sure they've got a better successor. Be that successor, if necessary.<br /> <br /> -Bend destiny so that everyone gets a bit more Serenity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T15:25:38-08:00","id":809145,"title":"","content":"Re: sanitation, depending on how &quot;real&quot; we wanted to get, a few links below on sanitation / water and how useful implementations on a ancient/preindustrial tech base might have been below:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cam.ac.uk/research/news/roman-toilets-gave-no-clear-health-benefit-and-romanisation-actually-spread-parasites\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cam.ac.uk/research/news/r...read-parasites</a> -<br /> <br /> &quot;Piers Mitchell said: \u201cModern research has shown that toilets, clean drinking water and removing faeces from the streets all decrease risk of infectious disease and parasites. So we might expect the prevalence of faecal oral parasites such as whipworm and roundworm to drop in Roman times \u2013 yet we find a gradual increase. The question is why?\u201d <br /> One possibility Mitchell offers is that it may have actually been the warm communal waters of the bathhouses that helped spread the parasitic worms. Water was infrequently changed in some baths, and a scum would build on the surface from human dirt and cosmetics. \u201cClearly, not all Roman baths were as clean as they might have been,\u201d said Mitchell.&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.alternatehistory.com/discussion/archive/index.php/t-154948.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.alternatehistory.com/disc.../t-154948.html</a> - <br /> <br /> Question: &quot;How much would medieval Europe change if they had the custom of cooking any water before drinking it?&quot; <br /> One Answer: &quot;It's hard to say, but probably not as much as we would think. From analysis of latrine contents it seems that the big issue was parasite load, not so much waterborne diseases. We can only speculate how much it would do for people's health....&quot;<br /> <br /> Followup: &quot;I must admit that I'm honestly surprised that waterborn parasites can stand boiling water while viruses and bacteria die.&quot;<br /> <br /> Followup Answer: &quot;What would lead you to that conclusion? It's far more likely that it simply reflects prevalence. It looks like there wasn't that much of Montezuma's revenge around, compared to other nasties. In the last book I read, they were completely uncertain why, but it's not an unknown phenomenon. bacteria have their own ecology, and under some circumstances they don't thrive.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/blogs/quora/2013/05/21/medieval_europe_why_was_water_the_most_popular_drink.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://compote.slate.com/images/c462a1b5-208e-486b-9645-31b7e19dd854.jpg?width=1560\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/blogs/quora/2013/05/21/medieval_europe_why_was_water_the_most_popular_drink.html\" target=\"_blank\"> What Was the Drink of Choice in Medieval Europe? </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/blogs/quora/2013/05/21/medieval_europe_why_was_water_the_most_popular_drink.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.slate.com/blogs/quora/2013/05/21/medieval_europe_why_was_water_the_most_popular_drink.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This question originally appeared on Quora. Answer by Tim O'Neill, medievalist: </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> At the same time, per Grabowski, the idea was- <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/RealmTechnologicalLevels\" target=\"_blank\">http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Sp...ologicalLevels</a><br /> <br /> &quot;I think Exalted's world lends itself to a fairly high quality if general well-being. There are some very good books on natural health floating around, and there are many lucky charms and efficacious prayers and magic tubers and whatnot. You can be really screwed if you suffer major physical trauma, because their surgery is mediocre (the have anasthetic and some equivalent to germ theory but not much else) but opportunistic ailments, parasites and so on are probably rather uncommon outside of crushing urban population densities and other environments of pervasive poverty.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Fits with the image that the Age of Sorrows isn't really exactly the Age of Sickly, Stunted People, esp. maybe combined with the kind of nutritional plenitude that the levels of harvests, land, magically improved crops, might suggest. They have other problems, generally?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T15:29:52-08:00","id":809151,"title":"","content":"Hm, true, agricultural concerns are probably a bit lesser when there's literal harvest gods that can tell people &quot;This is how to get the best yield out of your crop for this year&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T15:47:52-08:00","id":809167,"title":"","content":"I'm actually going to commit some balls-out heresy here and say that I'm not sure I want to agree with Grabowski on this subject. That page has a lot of really neat observations from him and there's some great ideas floating around in it, but he keeps coming back to the idea that the First Age was one of high technology and that the current era should be viewed as populated and governed by the inheritors of that knowledge. I'm willing to brave the torch-and-pitchfork crowd to say that maybe 3E doesn't make the same assumptions, and that might be a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T15:53:03-08:00","id":809171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809095#post809095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That actually lends itself to an often unexamined concern of improving living standards, since you also need to overcome the prejudices of the authorities concerning whether people of a certain class and rank should even be allowed to have access to certain benefits and luxuries. It's no good building a thing if you're going to have people who are too powerful for you to merely ignore work dilligently to tear it down again. It's like the difference between giving a certain section of the population the right to vote and preventing local government from introducing all kinds of arbitrary restrictions on registering to exercise that right. Or, for a more contemporary example that relates directly to one of these subjects; you can make schools available, but also have to ensure that people won't be targeted for attacks if they attend them.</div> </div> </div> </div>See also: the etymology of the word &quot;bulldozer.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:00:56-08:00","id":809175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809128#post809128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any talk of using Solar Charms to influence society at large should keep in mind how dependent so many things are on the general social system now. People are not mere puppets to the first Solar who speaks to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For good or ill, Chejop is right. It's pretty darned easy for a Social-Fu Solar to convert basically anyone who doesn't have magic backing it up. They can't recite a limerick and make a Wyld Hunt lay down its arms or anything, but if they can engage them in a few scenes of peaceful speech, they will flip right around to the Solar's way of thinking.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I think it can generally be said that you need to be on good working terms with the local gods. Maybe that's regular sacrifice and scheduled worship days. Maybe that's the threat of violence. A smart Twilight will lean on the former, but telegraph the possibility of the latter indirectly once they have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:05:24-08:00","id":809180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809167#post809167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually going to commit some balls-out heresy here and say that I'm not sure I want to agree with Grabowski on this subject. That page has a lot of really neat observations from him and there's some great ideas floating around in it, but he keeps coming back to the idea that the First Age was one of high technology and that the current era should be viewed as populated and governed by the inheritors of that knowledge. I'm willing to brave the torch-and-pitchfork crowd to say that maybe 3E doesn't make the same assumptions, and that might be a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there are areas of Creation, like the Realm and Lookshy, that are being govern by the inheritors of First Age Knowledge. Though, I imagine the Realm having a slightly higher standard of living than Lookshy. The Seventh Legion probably invested most of their resources on artifacts of strategic importance than the comfort of their citizens. <br /> <br /> However, this standard of living is not consistent throughout all of Creation. Some cities may have a great water treatment system, but other cities throw their shit on the streets. A lot of knowledge was lost after the Usurpation and the Great Contagion. Even if someone could read Old Realm, doesn't mean that they could understand what the book is talking about. I can read English, but a technical document on lithium battery usage in cell phone technology would be beyond me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:12:26-08:00","id":809181,"title":"","content":"While we're on this subject: I liked some of the mechanical ideas to the provisional revised version of Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe, but I'm ultimately glad that such a Charm didn't make it in, especially with the social system we got. Even with the kind of setup the Charm required, making sweeping changes to pervasive social attitudes should be more than a single Charm targeted at a single person. I imagined complications to the Charm before, but I can say that I'm more satisfied with applying them outside of a context in which you got Sova to start letting go of hate for Yugash by getting some of the National Tripartite Council to like you. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if they can engage them in a few scenes of peaceful speech, they will flip right around to the Solar's way of thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div> How in blue blazes do they manage that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:33:29-08:00","id":809192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809181#post809181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're on this subject: I liked some of the mechanical ideas to the provisional revised version of Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe, but I'm ultimately glad that such a Charm didn't make it in, especially with the social system we got. Even with the kind of setup the Charm required, making sweeping changes to pervasive social attitudes should be more than a single Charm targeted at a single person. I imagined complications to the Charm before, but I can say that I'm more satisfied with applying them outside of a context in which you got Sova to start letting go of hate for Yugash by getting some of the National Tripartite Council to like you. How in blue blazes do they manage that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's called roleplaying. Some people who play this game actually do it.<br /> &lt;/facetious&gt;<br /> <br /> Nobody needs to know the Social-Fu master is a Lawgiver until it's too late. Alternately, you can allow yourself to be captured and then talk too much while the Night Caste waits around to bail you out if stuff gets cray-cray. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:37:27-08:00","id":809198,"title":"","content":"I think the objection was to the notion that a couple scenes of conversation are all that's necessary to rewrite someone's beliefs wholesale. That doesn't seem to be either the intent or the typical result of the 3E social influence system. Thank goodness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:50:39-08:00","id":809261,"title":"","content":"I propose that exalted presents an alternate way to to raise the standard of living, through a <b>celestial revolution</b>. <br /> <br /> The core concept of the celestial revolution is the idea of the &quot;god as citizen&quot;. Imagine a kingdom where these godstake an active role in the nation. Road gods travel and maintain their individual routes, meeting with travellers and collecting prayer tolls, then return to the bureau of transportation to discuss current affairs with the local eclipse and mortal urban planners. The gods of metalworking each maintain their own temple forge, and wealthy mortals fall over each other competing to own a masterwork weapon forged by a literal god. The gods of sanitation, delighted to have a relevant portfolio again in the squalor of the second age, oversee a system of canals and water sources, cleaned by local water elementals. The gods of the field wander through great agricultural plantation, assisting mortal farmers to grow magnificent crops, and sometimes even helping to harvest fields as part of a great harvest festival. <br /> <br /> There are any number of gods that want to take a more active hand in the world, but are hampered by their celestial rivals or divine law. There are any number of gods with portfolios lost to the various cataclysms who would love to have worshipers and relevance again, and surely even some of the gods living in the slums of yu shan might be willing to leave to take up a position in a solars court. Furthermore, Solars have the authority to grant spirits divine permission to begin meddling in the world under the creation ruling mandate - if the solar rules some aspects of their domain through divine lieutenants who just happen to be the little gods who would oversee that domain, the laws of heaven cannot object. If the solars are sufficiently powerful to back up such a claim, they might even declare their citizen gods exempt from their responsibilities to the ailing celestial bureaucracy under similar laws; Heaven does not rule creation or the solars, and hence it does not rule their servants. This would, presumably, have consequences.<br /> <br /> Here's how I imagine it works: The solars actively recruit gods who would be enticed by this proposal, refugee gods and the like, and offer them a bargain: They may come and take up a vacant portfolio in the solars kingdom, as though it were a terrestrial court. they are guaranteed a certain amount of festivals and worshipers under the state calendar, and they are entitled to take an active hand in the management of their domain as long as they do so in a way that supports their kingdom, and that they don't take any action to undermine their new kingdom. In exchange, they are required to spend a certain amount of their efforts actively supporting the kingdom (a road god must work to maintain his roads, a god of craft must spend a certain amount of time labouring in his chosen craft, or must teach a certain number of apprentices each year, a medicine god must spend one week in every month working as a physician in the hospital).<br /> <br /> It's a harder bargain at first, hence the need to approach more desparate gods, but as these newcomers gain in power and stature and reliable worship, other gods are likely to come on board. In time, the goal is to bring the little gods into the fold of society as active citizens of the new state.<br /> <br /> In order to stop the system stagnating, preventing both gods and mortals from becoming complacent about divinity and worship, I came up with a final clause in the bargain: each year, during the calibration, every citizen god with sufficient power to do so must grant a permanent endowment to a mortal worshiper who has pleased it. This grants mortals the prospect of tangible rewards for their fidelity, and encourages the gods compete with each other for these abundant prayers.<br /> <br /> While this system would provide obvious and tangible benefits to the gods who participated, and to the nation as a whole, I think it also provides any number of story hooks where things do not go as planned, or where there are divine consequences for messing with the celestial order. Gods are not human and their idea of what constitutes action for the good of the city would sometimes be unthinkably odd. Gods who are left out of this new order would be jealous, desperate, or furious, and celestial courts stripped of some of their authority are unlikely to take it lying down. Local powers would have rather strong feelings about their new neighbour and powerful organisations (not to mention the immaculate order) would move against this divine affront.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10317-skina-stonedottir","name":"Skina Stonedottir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10317_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:54:48-08:00","id":809265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skina Stonedottir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809261#post809261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I propose that exalted presents an alternate way to to raise the standard of living, through a <b>celestial revolution</b>. <br /> <br /> The core concept of the celestial revolution is the idea of the &amp;quot;god as citizen&amp;quot;. Imagine a kingdom where these godstake an active role in the na