er them a bargain: They may come and take up a vacant portfolio in the solars kingdom, as though it were a terrestrial court. they are guaranteed a certain amount of festivals and worshipers under the state calendar, and they are entitled to take an active hand in the management of their domain as long as they do so in a way that supports their kingdom, and that they don't take any action to undermine their new kingdom. In exchange, they are required to spend a certain amount of their efforts actively supporting the kingdom (a road god must work to maintain his roads, a god of craft must spend a certain amount of time labouring in his chosen craft, or must teach a certain number of apprentices each year, a medicine god must spend one week in every month working as a physician in the hospital).<br /> <br /> It's a harder bargain at first, hence the need to approach more desparate gods, but as these newcomers gain in power and stature and reliable worship, other gods are likely to come on board. In time, the goal is to bring the little gods into the fold of society as active citizens of the new state.<br /> <br /> In order to stop the system stagnating, preventing both gods and mortals from becoming complacent about divinity and worship, I came up with a final clause in the bargain: each year, during the calibration, every citizen god with sufficient power to do so must grant a permanent endowment to a mortal worshiper who has pleased it. This grants mortals the prospect of tangible rewards for their fidelity, and encourages the gods compete with each other for these abundant prayers.<br /> <br /> While this system would provide obvious and tangible benefits to the gods who participated, and to the nation as a whole, I think it also provides any number of story hooks where things do not go as planned, or where there are divine consequences for messing with the celestial order. Gods are not human and their idea of what constitutes action for the good of the city would sometimes be unthinkably odd. Gods who are left out of this new order would be jealous, desperate, or furious, and celestial courts stripped of some of their authority are unlikely to take it lying down. Local powers would have rather strong feelings about their new neighbour and powerful organisations (not to mention the immaculate order) would move against this divine affront.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may steal this idea for a Zenith concept I have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T18:06:56-08:00","id":809270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the objection was to the notion that a couple scenes of conversation are all that's necessary to rewrite someone's beliefs wholesale. That doesn't seem to be either the intent or the typical result of the 3E social influence system. Thank goodness.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could probably do it with Celestial Bliss Trick.<br /> <br /> A sensible ST won't allow that Charm, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T20:19:19-08:00","id":809325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skina Stonedottir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809261#post809261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[snip]</div> </div> </div> </div>I did that with a Zenith of mine once. It started as part of the settlement where all these gods gave up the demesnes and lost manses they owned in the area for geomantic infrastructure. In exchange they got representation in the various &quot;advisory&quot; councils that formed the major legislative bodies of the government and the state build and maintained holy cities where Wyld Revocation allowed ambrosia to form.<br /> <br /> There were a few issues. One of the big ones was the divine legions stalling immensely when they when they were supposed to be fighting celestial opponents. There was the mandate of Heaven and laws of Heaven thing of course, but a lot of them did not like the thought of actually dying against GET. This was a bigger problem then it might otherwise be because the divine legions were also the backbone of the army while the mortal legions and the artisans were teching up from Solar training charms.<br /> <br /> Then there was the issue of the prayer calendar. It really was a zero sum game unless the population got bigger. So as the system got bigger and more important and influential gods started wanting a piece it had to come from less powerful gods which neither they nor the Zenith liked. This led to a policy of aggressive diplomacy on the borders to annex new tax prayers and expand the prayer boosting geomancy. Which brought the gods of the new territory into the fold and made the nation an even more attractive prospect for gods. It also made the neighbors uneasy and started attracting Sidereal and Infernal saboteurs and assassins like a magnet. Never really solved this problem.<br /> <br /> After that there was Heaven to consider. The nations Heavenly lobby was suddenly very rich and had a huge vested interest in making sure the Zenith didn't start getting into trouble. The Gold Faction held it up as an example of how things were supposed to go, the Bronze could see all the flaws threatening to make the thing collapse into even more chaos than before, and a lot of portfolios were getting reshuffled.<br /> <br /> Finally, the was the increasing prayer tax burden on the people. It made sense to switch from currency taxes to ambrosia meaning mortals needed to pray a certain amount to pay their taxes. This was obviously very hard to keep track of. A proposed solution was to have slightly different prayers based on area so that you could track if a region wasn't meeting quota because some minor god of taxation in the area wasn't getting enough. However the people also had to pray more when government expenses went up. It started doing unpleasant things to their actual faith which was important to the Zenith.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There were other problems like the Lintha citizens holding on to demon worship for cultural reasons and the complex legal fictions required to give Jadeborn actual influence without triggering the Geas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 01-14-2016, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T00:15:42-08:00","id":809409,"title":"","content":"I think, regarding the &quot;Converting people into worshipful lackeys&quot; conversation, that in 3e the problem becomes considerably more nuanced. That is to say, you can tag people with all sorts of ridiculous Intimacies and get them to do your will relatively easy, but it doesn't overwrite their personalities - it causes some new principle they care about in addition to what they already cared about. A noble might respect you, fear you, lust for you, and so forth, and those feelings motivates him to do as you say - but unless you pay careful attention and set up more Intimacies beyond just &quot;love/admire/respect the Solar&quot;, he'll have no real incentive to not do bad things beyond &quot;The Solar told me not to&quot;.<br /> <br /> So it comes back, I think, to roleplaying and no one Charm solving everything. You can with time and effort educate the aristocracy in your new system of governance, but I think an ST worth their salt will have an easier time coming up with realistic complications to that in 3e. Noble 1 is very greedy (Principle: Collect more money) and might endorse the new system but still take bribes on the side, Noble 2 cares only for her children, Noble 3 is religious and resents both family ties and monetary wealth as material trappings, and so forth. You might be able to get them all to respect you, personally, or some abstract principle. That doesn't mean they'll necessarily play nice with each other, or with the local populace.<br /> <br /> You can still convince them play nice, obviously, but that's going to be a story in itself, not just a few rolls - especially since there often is no real one-size-fits-all solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2196-riklurt","name":"Riklurt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T01:24:11-08:00","id":809433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's called roleplaying. Some people who play this game actually do it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would prefer an actual breakdown of how it works in the system that models people's motivations and relationships. This idea that Solars are able to make puppets of people after a few scenes of listening to them is an old chestnut, so it won't die easily, but people coming in to Third Edition really do need to look at the social system, look at the actual Charms Solars have, and recognise how even mortals won't be swayed to give their lives to somebody with a 20 die pool if they have no investment in what that speaker is selling, let alone if they have active hostilities. That's before one even gets to what kinds of Charms or Merits a member of the Wyld Hunt might have to stay the course. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could probably do it with Celestial Bliss Trick</div> </div> </div> </div> First rule of the Wyld Hunt; don't fuck the Anathema. Second rule of the Wyld Hunt: Intimacies can only be used to support actions related to their characteristics, and &quot;Lust&quot; has fairly limited applications, and Decision Points are still a thing so somebody with a Defining Intimacy based on things like killing Anathema (which, as a member of the Wyld Hunt, you should have) can spend Willpower to ignore anything you might be impelled towards by that lust. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sensible ST won't allow that Charm, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can assure you, I am quite the true Scotsman. Why, I even find the sound of bagpipe music to be rather pleasant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T01:37:42-08:00","id":809441,"title":"","content":"Huh?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where the no-true-Scotsman is supposed to be here.<br /> <br /> And for what it's worth, I wasn't really talking about the Wyld Hunt. I know that's where the conversation started, but it's a single narrow case and I'm not terribly interested in it.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying, if you wanna rewrite someone's beliefs wholesale in a few scenes, you can probably do it with Celestial Bliss Trick.<br /> <br /> Without that one broken Charm, though, I think you'll have a fair bit of trouble brainwashing people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T01:49:26-08:00","id":809446,"title":"","content":"As well as talking about changing the external environment to improve living conditions, how about improving the people?<br /> <br /> In my game, PCs used training charms to teach large numbers of people Craft, Survival, Stamina and so forth, making them healthier and better able to produce stuff. And Charisma and Socialise 4... so they get on well with each other!<br /> But the biggest thing was a mighty project that gave all the people in their kingdom Extended Lifespan and Exalted Healing, so they no longer die of disease.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T02:01:26-08:00","id":809451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure where the no-true-Scotsman is supposed to be here.</div> </div> </div> </div> Were I a Storyteller, I would have no objection to the Charm, so I suppose I'm not sensible. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you wanna rewrite someone's beliefs wholesale in a few scenes, you can probably do it with Celestial Bliss Trick.</div> </div> </div> </div> Break that down for me; the steps between a single Defining Tie, and altering a person's beliefs wholesale. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">one broken Charm</div> </div> </div> </div> That is useless unless people will have sex with you. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">you'll have a fair bit of trouble brainwashing people</div> </div> </div> </div> I think you'll have a fair bit of trouble brainwashing people in all cases, because that's not the paradigm that social influence works off of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T02:44:11-08:00","id":809456,"title":"","content":"Do you know one thing that was a really significant part of the Industrial Revolution, significant to people's living standards, and often overlooked? Clothing. Not just the machine-assited processing of textiles, but also the finishing of those textiles as full articles. Textiles (especially wool) have been a major commodity for centuries, but a big part of the Industrial Revolution was making it cheaper and more practical for people from every level of society to own multiple sets of decently made clothes. That has several implications beyond mere vanity; having several of them means you can more easily have laundered clothes on a regular basis which is important for general hygiene and social interaction, and their decent quality means they're comfortable, warm, and non-abrasive enough to reduce incidence of skin diseases. You want to improve people's quality of life, find a way to get them some nice duds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T07:03:56-08:00","id":809558,"title":"","content":"I'll also toss in Cheap and Good Lighting.<br /> <br /> without a light source that is both strong and cheap, you are largely limited to daylight hours for most work and most active time for people.<br /> <br /> with cheap lighting you have the capacity to increase those hours allowing either more work at a primary job (possibly even a night shift, allowing the production of goods to double for a given space) or increase the non-physical labor time of the population (aka improving education and socializing).<br /> <br /> Food, clean water, clean environment, light, stable laws and government, encouragement of innovation and efficiency. Then you have increasing specialization, increasing productivity and generally reach the point of having an upward spiral as long as you can maintain it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T07:19:02-08:00","id":809565,"title":"","content":"Oh, lighting's easy. Just cultivate bioluminescent trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T07:37:15-08:00","id":809572,"title":"","content":"Turn everyone into sentient undead - remove all possible issues with the quality of life instantly and permanently!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T07:43:03-08:00","id":809576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809572#post809572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turn everyone into sentient undead - remove all possible issues with the quality of life instantly and permanently!</div> </div> </div> </div>Whelp, time to head over to the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build\">What SHOULD an Abyssal be able to build?</a>&quot; thread. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T08:01:26-08:00","id":809583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809576#post809576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whelp, time to head over to the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build\">What SHOULD an Abyssal be able to build?</a>&quot; thread. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just where I came from <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T11:29:12-08:00","id":809739,"title":"","content":"As far as Craft go, Geomancy seems like a good idea. Among the example Hearthstones in the core book, there are various that can improve quality of life for miles. Then maybe you augment and/or extend the effect with an Artifact or Sorcerous Working and things should start to get quite good for the people living there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T12:09:43-08:00","id":809771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809451#post809451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Were I a Storyteller, I would have no objection to the Charm, so I suppose I'm not sensible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not on this point, at least. A big part of being a sensible ST is banning the stuff that needs banning.<br /> <br /> (Even if you disagree with this, it's not a no-true-Scotsman any more than &quot;no true Scotsman would vote against independence&quot;. The fallacy in the no-true-Scotsman is in redefining Scottishness, and I'm working off a coherent definition of sensible STing here.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809451#post809451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Break that down for me; the steps between a single Defining Tie, and altering a person's beliefs wholesale.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, you give them the Defining Tie. Then, since &quot;Defining Intimacies represent the most important things in a character\u2019s life, the relationships or beliefs that they place above all others and refuse to compromise. Defining Intimacies influence the greater part of a character\u2019s behavior in all fields of life.&quot; you're actually done.<br /> <br /> You can persuade them to do almost anything, and unless they've got opposed Defining Intimacies (think they might need two: one to boost defense, on for the decision point) they're gonna do it. Beating a non-magical character's Resolve is easy, especially with the autosuccesses from CBT.<br /> <br /> But to make it stick once CBT's brainwashing wears off, you'll want to make more social influence attempts. Fortunately, with a Defining Intimacy you can weaken or strengthen whatever Intimacies you want with simple rolls. Most people have very little wp and it regenerates slowly. Plus they don't use it on every roll. So you can easily rewrite their whole list of Intimacies over a few scenes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809451#post809451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is useless unless people will have sex with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Clearly the solution is that nobody ever have sex with anyone who might be a Solar, in case their brain is magically overwritten by sex magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T13:18:24-08:00","id":809816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> since &quot;Defining Intimacies represent the most important things in a character\u2019s life, the relationships or beliefs that they place above all others and refuse to compromise. Defining Intimacies influence the greater part of a character\u2019s behavior in all fields of life.&quot; you're actually done.</div> </div> </div> </div> I suppose making additions to a person's beliefs and actions even while all of the ones they had before is <i>technically</i> altering them, even if a lot of their behaviour remains the same. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can persuade them to do almost anything</div> </div> </div> </div> Nnnno you can't. You can persuade them to do things relevant to the Intimacy, and persuade actions need to make arguments that actually coherently incorporate the Intimacy. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortunately, with a Defining Intimacy you can weaken or strengthen whatever Intimacies you want with simple rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div> Again, no; they'd have to be things that the Intimacy you're trying to use can reasonably be argued to support or oppose. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly the solution is that nobody ever have sex with anyone who might be a Solar</div> </div> </div> </div> My point was more about the fact that the Solar can't instill the Intimacy with impunity; that there's a necessary action they need to engage with that may be undesirable or impractical or outright fail under particular circumstances. You discounted the reference to the Wyld Hunt outright, and yet it's a pretty significant example of an occasion in which a Solar can't actually use this Charm to influence people at all. For that matter, this whole thread is concerned with the question of a Solar effecting widespread social change; are you suggesting that a Solar is going to try, or be capable of; having sex with everybody in their society in order to ensure that they're all on the same page? It's not a question of &quot;nobody should ever have sex&quot;, it's &quot;does somebody want to have sex with you specifically?&quot;. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">in case their brain is magically overwritten by sex magic</div> </div> </div> </div> Because sex that doesn't involve the elevated prowess of the Solars doesn't involve any kind of major emotional upheavals that might influence how people act. Same with how if a Solar made a Pixar movie, you're not crying because they made a legitimately superior form of Inside Out, you're crying because they used insidious cry magic on you. Damn those Solars and their violation of the unencroachable transcendent rational box that is your brain, forcing it to act like a biochemical meat ball calibrated for interpersonal interactions!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T13:25:11-08:00","id":809819,"title":"","content":"A defining Intimacy of lust towards you can justify almost any influence attack, I think.<br /> <br /> And I'm obviously not talking about widespread social change. This is a tangent. I'm talking about replacing the minds of individual people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809816#post809816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same with how if a Solar made a Pixar movie, you're not crying because they made a legitimately superior form of Inside Out, you're crying because they used insidious cry magic on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>If &quot;crying about how good their movie is&quot; became the defining element of my personality for weeks, then yes. That's insidious cry magic.<br /> <br /> No matter how it's flavoured, that's brainwashing. Actually, that's a lot more powerful than any real-world form of brainwashing.<br /> <br /> And it's also hugely overpowered, incidentally, in a game that mostly tries to keep social influence sensible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T14:46:15-08:00","id":809854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809819#post809819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A defining Intimacy of lust towards you can justify almost any influence attack, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't enter a Decision Point if someone's trying to degrade a Major or Defining Intimacy. You can just spend a WP to resist. Decision Points can only be used to get someone to take an action.<br /> <br /> If your goal is to get the Guild factor to release his slaves, CBT can get you there. If your goal is to convince him that slavery is evil and he ought to share his wealth with the poor, I hope you like giving blowjobs, 'cos it's gonna take a while.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809819#post809819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And I'm obviously not talking about widespread social change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure you are. If just a handful of leaders change their position on an issue, that could mean massive changes for society. Think of Lyndon Johnson and the Civil Rights Act, or Merkel dealing with the refugee crisis - and those are leaders in democracies, not monarchies. A seductress who managed to get Henry VIII or Charlemagne wrapped around her finger would effectively rule the nation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For Industrial Revolution-ing a society, I'm still going to stick with sorcerous workings. Mass-produce a few thousand crude totems, then cast a Working so that they grant +2 Resistance to anyone in line of sight to them and a soft glowing light at night - boom, you've radically minimized the spread of disease and got the light-bulb / street lights all through your city. Work the local grain into producing ridiculously huge harvests, Work the local fish into growing three times their normal size, Work a local vineyard into producing grapes made of pure silver - 8 XP and we're well into paradise, by Creation's standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T14:51:29-08:00","id":809857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809854#post809854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't enter a Decision Point if someone's trying to degrade a Major or Defining Intimacy. You can just spend a WP to resist. Decision Points can only be used to get someone to take an action.. <br /> <br /> If your goal is to get the Guild factor to release his slaves, CBT can get you there. If your goal is to convince him that slavery is evil and he ought to share his wealth with the poor, I hope you like giving blowjobs, 'cos it's gonna take a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>That paragraph was specifically about persuade actions. I talk about other influence in the next paragraph.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809854#post809854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure you are. If just a handful of leaders change their position on an issue, that could mean massive changes for society. Think of Lyndon Johnson and the Civil Rights Act, or Merkel dealing with the refugee crisis - and those are leaders in democracies, not monarchies. A seductress who managed to get Henry VIII or Charlemagne wrapped around her finger would effectively rule the nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, now you're talking about widespread social change. I'm not, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T16:14:23-08:00","id":809894,"title":"","content":"One obvious way to improve living standards is to introduce high-yield grains. Seriously. Most medieval or earlier grains only yielded between 3:1 to 6:1: plant one seed, get six back. Modern high-yield grains give 50:1, and a competent sorceror can create such grains with a Terrestrial working, Ambition 2 at the outside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:18:46-08:00","id":810042,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's been said, didn't see it, but note that the early industrial revolution didn't <i>improve</i> most people's stnadard of living. Cities were deathtraps (seriously, London had a negative population growth if you didn't count immigration) vast numbers of individuasl found their livilihoods taken from them by the new industrial order etc, etc. So a major part of your goal may be specifically <i>not</i> going in that direction which is actually pretty attainable with even terrestrial sorcerous workings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T21:06:24-08:00","id":810064,"title":"","content":"The average age of a man in London in the early 19th century was 17, as infant and child mortality was so high, so you're right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T00:16:45-08:00","id":810123,"title":"","content":"I have never seen any player try to save Creation by building the Malfean Mills, no.<br /> <br /> But there is a pronounced tendency to usher in a new Age/recall the First Age along lines of really distinctly trying to emulate real-world technological progress, and I really like this thread for trying to imagine other ways to improve the lot of the common Mortal in more unique directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T00:29:20-08:00","id":810125,"title":"","content":"I agree. For one thing, modern technology often requires institutions, ways of thinking, and infrastructure that isn't available in Creation, so it's not really feasible. Plus of course, it rather turns it into a different game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T05:41:14-08:00","id":810189,"title":"","content":"Something Grabowski once wrote about that stands out to me was the idea that part of why the First Age didn't industrialize is because it wasn't based on the need to organize large numbers of people to accomplish important tasks. Something I take from this is how so many pre-modern societies engaged in various forms of mandatory labour for the people living within them as a necessary means of constructing large scale monuments or infrastructure, the likes of which tends to make the name of a lot of those civilizations. It gets me thinking of the alternatives, which generally comes to me in a form of &quot;a Solar, Lunar, a few Dragon Blooded, and a relatively small elite work force trained and coordinated by the Solar, equipped with superior tools and supplemented by a bit of sorcerous aid such as bound demons, can manage the work of building a continent spanning roadway by themselves&quot;.<br /> <br /> From there, you're creating a social and economic premise sufficiently different from the real life circumstances that promoted industrialisation (a lot of which had more to do with adaptations for imperialism and land enclosure than the invention of the steam engine, which I assess would have amounted to an irrelevant curiosity for the wealthy and intellectual in any other circumstances) that it isn't difficult to find ways for people to operate without the need for large amounts of automated machinery to change the work dynamic.<br /> <br /> I still picture things like factory-cathedrals existing, but more as the kinds of facilities you need to produce the custom parts for a spacecraft (which I'm pretty sure was what they were generally supposed to be anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:17:05-08:00","id":812110,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking a lot about Lore and its power to change Creation. There have been a few mentions of how crappy Tome-Rearing Gesture is, and that made me think about books a little more and why they're so important. It's been ages since I last read it, but Neal Stephenson 's <i>Diamond Age </i>explores the power of &quot;The Young Lady's Illustrated Primer,&quot; a sort of book that teaches everything from basic literacy, self-esteem, and critical thinking to more advanced lessons and values, and which some desire as a powerful instrument of revolution. And of course we have real books that some people say have changed their lives and that have overthrown cultures and leaders. Further, there's a lot of debate over what children should learn, how they should learn it, and who should teach it, and not just from the standpoint of how to optimally get knowledge into brains. Finally, a lot of the change discussed in this thread is only helpful if people accept it (whether that means leaders allowing change or common folk permitting it in their lives) and learn how to benefit from it - technology and infrastructure aren't worth much sitting around unused. Or worse, the Solar might create something other than what she intended - her system of roads might further enrich and empower the Guild, for example, spreading their abuses to new corners of Creation, while others don't take advantage of the opportunities faster, safer travel can create.<br /> <br /> So education, particularly through books, strikes me as one of the greatest powers of the Solar. She can come up with a glorious, ennobling philosophy. She can collect lost lore and blaze new paths. From there she has to spread these beliefs, with people and books as her primary means more often than not. This is where I find Tome-Rearing Gesture to be interesting - in some place near the edge of the world or troubled by a pocket of Wyld, she can pull out her great work and let her beliefs take root. Of course she could have had books printed up and bound before she set out, but hey, you rarely know where you'll end up or what you'll find. Anyway, whatever improvements the Solar envisions, she needs to send people out into the world armed with her ideals and her words so that people can learn to take advantage of what she has made and also to build on her achievements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:19:19-08:00","id":812112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=812110#post812110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So education, particularly through books, strikes me as one of the greatest powers of the Solar. She can come up with a glorious, ennobling philosophy. She can collect lost lore and blaze new paths. From there she has to spread these beliefs, with people and books as her primary means more often than not. This is where I find Tome-Rearing Gesture to be interesting - in some place near the edge of the world or troubled by a pocket of Wyld, she can pull out her great work and let her beliefs take root. Of course she could have had books printed up and bound before she set out, but hey, you rarely know where you'll end up or what you'll find. Anyway, whatever improvements the Solar envisions, she needs to send people out into the world armed with her ideals and her words so that people can learn to take advantage of what she has made and also to build on her achievements.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my current Ex2 Twilight's motivation. I was really excited to see the Ex3 Lore, because it fit that character so well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:49:19-08:00","id":812138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=812110#post812110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking a lot about Lore and its power to change Creation. There have been a few mentions of how crappy Tome-Rearing Gesture is, and that made me think about books a little more and why they're so important. It's been ages since I last read it, but Neal Stephenson 's <i>Diamond Age </i>explores the power of &quot;The Young Lady's Illustrated Primer,&quot; a sort of book that teaches everything from basic literacy, self-esteem, and critical thinking to more advanced lessons and values, and which some desire as a powerful instrument of revolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loved <i>Diamond Age</i>. Of course, the reason that the <i>Primer </i>is so powerful is that it's far more than just a book.<br /> <br /> Not that you'll find me speaking ill of books, ever. But <i>Tome-Rearing Gesture</i> doesn't do anything that the character couldn't already do with it's prerequisites, <i>Whirling Brush Method, </i>and a day off. It gets pegged as indulgent wish-fulfillment for writers because, well, that's all it really is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T15:38:51-08:00","id":812183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=812138#post812138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Loved <i>Diamond Age</i>. Of course, the reason that the <i>Primer </i>is so powerful is that it's far more than just a book.<br /> <br /> Not that you'll find me speaking ill of books, ever. But <i>Tome-Rearing Gesture</i> doesn't do anything that the character couldn't already do with it's prerequisites, <i>Whirling Brush Method, </i>and a day off. It gets pegged as indulgent wish-fulfillment for writers because, well, that's all it really is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say something as powerful as the <i>Primer</i> ideally suits Creation anyway - a book so powerful that once it's out there in the world you just roll credits and assume humanity is forever changed is a bit much even for Solars. But a work that similarly aimed to motivate, enlighten, and teach makes sense. It wouldn't have every technique for building or farming or fighting disease known to man, but it would give people what they need to survive, learn faster, and adapt to their environment. It couldn't have the perfect code of laws for all places, but it could at least point people toward a more just and fruitful life.<br /> <br /> Something that grand could be pretty massive, which is where Tome-Rearing Gesture is handy. You want a sturdily bound book that can weather the touch of many hands over the course of generations, not a pile of pages. There are other ways to create books that can last, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T18:35:57-08:00","id":812266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=809819#post809819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A defining Intimacy of lust towards you can justify almost any influence attack, I think.<br /> <br /> And I'm obviously not talking about widespread social change. This is a tangent. I'm talking about replacing the minds of individual people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If &quot;crying about how good their movie is&quot; became the defining element of my personality for weeks, then yes. That's insidious cry magic.<br /> <br /> No matter how it's flavoured, that's brainwashing. Actually, that's a lot more powerful than any real-world form of brainwashing.<br /> <br /> And it's also hugely overpowered, incidentally, in a game that mostly tries to keep social influence sensible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> There\u2019s a game, its called Analogue: A Hate story. In that game something pretty awful happens to a main character that you learn about through reading their personal logs. Its not sexual and has that whole hindsight effect like the twist from the shining. The game is kind of A Handmaidens Tale in space. It fucked me up for like two weeks afterwards. I was near tears for the first two days. Like i felt super depressed and sad. That wasn\u2019t insidious brainwashing, that was a combination of good storycraft and the right target. I have heard and seen other people be affected that severly by other works of media with the same emotions and different ones. So uh i hereby dispel the notion of charms as insidious cry magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T19:16:17-08:00","id":812290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=808965#post808965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clean water is pretty easy actually. If the water is dirty, summon up some water cleaner elementals to clean the water for you. In Nexus's case you may want several dozen. If the God of Pollution or small gods of dirty water show up, kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is so sad.<br /> <br /> Really, think about it. Elementals in 3rd Edition are created when you summon them. You're making a being, an intelligent, self-aware being, whose entire existence is cleaning up human waste.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T02:20:53-08:00","id":812462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, think about it. Elementals in 3rd Edition are created when you summon them. You're making a being, an intelligent, self-aware being, whose entire existence is cleaning up human waste.</div> </div> </div> </div> Could be worse. <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X7HmltUWXgs\" data-code=\"X7HmltUWXgs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/X7HmltUWXgs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T05:56:07-08:00","id":812529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=812462#post812462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could <i>always</i> be worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:24:02-08:00","id":812779,"title":"","content":"If it was made to clean up human waste, it probably enjoys doing so. There are plenty of animals that love eating poop, it's not that far-fetched.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TavelGorge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=812266#post812266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s a game, its called Analogue: A Hate story. In that game something pretty awful happens to a main character that you learn about through reading their personal logs. Its not sexual and has that whole hindsight effect like the twist from the shining. The game is kind of A Handmaidens Tale in space. It fucked me up for like two weeks afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, really?<br /> <br /> Wow. That goes beyond anything I've seen from media before. Might have to play that game.<br /> <br /> Still, I don't think it sounds like a Defining Intimacy. Seems more like a super-successful Instill action. Defining Intimacies are things you can use to talk people into almost anything.<br /> <br /> CBT lets you bang someone so well that they'll murder their friends for you (unless their friendship or their moral code is Defining, which is unusual). I'm honestly surprised that people don't see it as scary, evil, brainwashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:48:37-08:00","id":812805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=812779#post812779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, really?<br /> <br /> Wow. That goes beyond anything I've seen from media before. Might have to play that game.<br /> <br /> Still, I don't think it sounds like a Defining Intimacy. Seems more like a super-successful Instill action. Defining Intimacies are things you can use to talk people into almost anything.<br /> <br /> CBT lets you bang someone so well that they'll murder their friends for you (unless their friendship or their moral code is Defining, which is unusual). I'm honestly surprised that people don't see it as scary, evil, brainwashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may not be the same for you. Im not sure id put Analogue up there as ground breaking or a game changing story. Undertale and Steven universe are both written better from my perspective. But thats the rub isnt it? It hit me hard and faded slow. <br /> <br /> My grandmother saw the exorcist when it first came out and it startled the shit out of her from that day on. Like she was actively afraid of scarey movies like it forever after. You know that scene in Looper, where the guy has to run to a place because theyre mutilating him in the past and his body parts just vanish and its basically a protracted action medical torture scene without gore? That did the same thing to me. It just shocked my system and left me feeling sick. When the shit did looper come out? Im still shakey typing out and remembering that one scene.<br /> <br /> These mundane examples are probaly defining or at least major intimacies that slowly downgraded out to minor or just vanished. Which is how CBT works. It hits hard and bleeds off. You couldnt really manipulate me through them now..but at the time? Maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:58:19-08:00","id":812817,"title":"","content":"I think that's a consequence of the argument that the Intimacy isn't instilled <i>by magic</i>, it's just the natural consequence of a mind-blowing orgasm. /eyeroll<br /> <br /> Which is completely ludicrous. If a Charm lets you skip past all the normal mechanics for Instilling a Defining Intimacy, then yeah it's magic brainwashing. If you then leverage that Intimacy to convince your paramour to do things they otherwise wouldn't consider doing (and why else would you use it?), you're engaging in emotional and psychological blackmail. Even if using the Charm itself isn't inherently reprehensible, the implications of <i>how it is meant to be used </i>basically paint the character as a sexual apex predator. For the same reason that nobody is going to take Tiger Warrior Training unless they plan to send men off to fight and die for them, nobody is going to take this unless they intend to engage in sexually-transmitted coercion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T19:37:05-08:00","id":813101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=812290#post812290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is so sad.<br /> <br /> Really, think about it. Elementals in 3rd Edition are created when you summon them. You're making a being, an intelligent, self-aware being, whose entire existence is cleaning up human waste.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The people who work at the dump near where I live make a killing.<br /> <br /> On the bright side you got a job and if people know whats good for them, good pay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T08:16:56-08:00","id":813382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=810189#post810189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something Grabowski once wrote about that stands out to me was the idea that part of why the First Age didn't industrialize is because it wasn't based on the need to organize large numbers of people to accomplish important tasks. Something I take from this is how so many pre-modern societies engaged in various forms of mandatory labour for the people living within them as a necessary means of constructing large scale monuments or infrastructure, the likes of which tends to make the name of a lot of those civilizations. It gets me thinking of the alternatives, which generally comes to me in a form of &amp;quot;a Solar, Lunar, a few Dragon Blooded, and a relatively small elite work force trained and coordinated by the Solar, equipped with superior tools and supplemented by a bit of sorcerous aid such as bound demons, can manage the work of building a continent spanning roadway by themselves&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> From there, you're creating a social and economic premise sufficiently different from the real life circumstances that promoted industrialisation (a lot of which had more to do with adaptations for imperialism and land enclosure than the invention of the steam engine, which I assess would have amounted to an irrelevant curiosity for the wealthy and intellectual in any other circumstances) that it isn't difficult to find ways for people to operate without the need for large amounts of automated machinery to change the work dynamic.<br /> <br /> I still picture things like factory-cathedrals existing, but more as the kinds of facilities you need to produce the custom parts for a spacecraft (which I'm pretty sure was what they were generally supposed to be anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is a thing I've been trying and failing to articulate for years. Kudos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T08:26:16-08:00","id":813388,"title":"","content":"&quot;Almost anything&quot; is an idiomatic phrase; it does not override the established system logic in which persuasions need to be connected to what the person's Intimacy is. A person with a Defining Tie of hate for the Realm can be persuaded to do extremely dangerous or costly things related to hate for the Realm, and nothing else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T09:30:34-08:00","id":813428,"title":"","content":"Say, what ingredient should I use if I want to invent some antibacterial soap and toothbrush in Creation ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T09:45:40-08:00","id":813438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=813428#post813428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say, what ingredient should I use if I want to invent some antibacterial soap and toothbrush in Creation ?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you just want a cleaning agent, I suggest garlic. Or, if smelling good is more important to you, maybe ginger would be better.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www2.hawaii.edu/~johnb/micro/m140/syllabus/week/handouts/m140.8.3.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www2.hawaii.edu/~johnb/micro/.../m140.8.3.html</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T09:58:51-08:00","id":813451,"title":"","content":"Products defined as antibotic are <a href=\"http://bigstory.ap.org/article/fda-says-germ-killing-soap-could-pose-health-risks\" target=\"_blank\">no more effective</a> at sanitation than regular soap and warm water for handwashing.<br /> <br /> To make soap, all you need is lye (wood ash is a common source of this) and a fat to bind it in (animal fat or olive oil works). It's not that soap is difficult to make, it's that you need to educate people that they need to frequently wash their hands with soap and warm water.<br /> <br /> For toothpaste, if you have <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natron\" target=\"_blank\">natron deposits</a>, you can grind it into a powder. When people mix it with water, it becomes a sort of salty paste to brush their teeth with. You can also promote nice breath by getting people to chomp on fennel after a meal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T10:12:08-08:00","id":813458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=813388#post813388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Almost anything&quot; is an idiomatic phrase; it does not override the established system logic in which persuasions need to be connected to what the person's Intimacy is. A person with a Defining Tie of hate for the Realm can be persuaded to do extremely dangerous or costly things related to hate for the Realm, and nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, a Defining Intimacy doesn't negate reason and foresight. &quot;Kill your family and I'll hump you again,&quot; suggests that immense risk and sacrifice will be necessary every time a hump is desired and that it's time to get some leverage over your lover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T10:45:14-08:00","id":813481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=813438#post813438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you just want a cleaning agent, I suggest garlic</div> </div> </div> </div>So garlic is both antibacterial, antifungal <i>and</i> antiviral, holy crap a Twilight better create a specie of garlic without the smell fast !<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T11:57:20-08:00","id":813530,"title":"","content":"Life is nanotechnology. Appropriate breeding and horticulture can produce extraordinarily powerful self-replicating infrastructure. Become a sorcerer-botanist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T12:52:36-08:00","id":813570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=812817#post812817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and why else would you use it?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking personally? My characters who are inclined to build intimacies via seduction are doing it primarily to protect themselves in the event of discovery, because intimacies of romantic feelings make excellent leverage for persuading people not to kill you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T04:19:51-08:00","id":814034,"title":"","content":"Really, while there's a lot of significance to the use of Intimacies in persuading people to act in ways they wouldn't otherwise be inclined to (and to <i>not</i> act in ways that they might; somebody can use that Defining Intimacy to resist attempts to persuade them to do something to harm you), one should also consider the fact that they're meant to represent what a person is actually interested in and inclined towards. You can rapidly give somebody a positive (or, rather, possessive) Defining Intimacy towards you and then simply let them act upon it of their own initiative. Plus, considering the fact that lust can be possessive rather than submissive, even if you are using it for persuasion, the characteristics of that interaction need not be coercive or withholding; you can be in a position to influence people from the role of their most beloved servant, prostrating yourself before them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T08:33:58-07:00","id":1107024,"title":"","content":"Permaculture is another thing that could be introduced. It's a form of food production that doesn't involved tilling; instead of taking prairie as a food source, you tame a forest, using tall, sun-loving nut trees, medium height partial shade-loving fruit trees, low, shade-loving berry bushes, and finally ground-cover herbs. Hunt the animals that come to the fringes, and you get meat as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T09:44:52-07:00","id":1107040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107024#post1107024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Permaculture is another thing that could be introduced. It's a form of food production that doesn't involved tilling; instead of taking prairie as a food source, you tame a forest, using tall, sun-loving nut trees, medium height partial shade-loving fruit trees, low, shade-loving berry bushes, and finally ground-cover herbs. Hunt the animals that come to the fringes, and you get meat as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh hell yes.<br /> <br /> and I remember this one. The three sisters. Planted by Native Americans.<br /> <br /> Here's a quote from the page:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Lora\">By the time European settlers arrived in America in the early 1600s, the Iroquois had been growing the \u201cthree sisters\u201d for over three centuries. The vegetable trio sustained the Native Americans both physically and spiritually. In legend, the plants were a gift from the gods, always to be grown together, eaten together, and celebrated together.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Lora\">Each of the sisters contributes something to the planting. Together, the sisters provide a balanced diet from a single planting. </span><ul><li>As older sisters often do, the corn offers the beans needed support.</li> <li>The beans, the giving sister, pull nitrogen from the air and bring it to the soil for the benefit of all three.</li> <li>As the beans grow through the tangle of squash vines and wind their way up the cornstalks into the sunlight, they hold the sisters close together.</li> <li>The large leaves of the sprawling squash protect the threesome by creating living mulch that shades the soil, keeping it cool and moist and preventing weeds.</li> <li>The prickly squash leaves also keep away raccoons, which don\u2019t like to step on them.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Lora\">Together, the three sisters provide both sustainable soil fertility as well as a heathly diet. Perfection!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 06-23-2017, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T10:05:35-07:00","id":1107045,"title":"","content":"Talking about seduction there are two examples in literature that have stuck with me, one i liked and one i hated<br /> <br /> The one i liked was in a Song of Ice and Fire when Arianne Martell seduced Ser Arys Oakheart making him break his vows and join in on her plot to get Myrcella on the throne.<br /> The one i hated was in the Three Musketeers when Milady brainwashes John Felton into freeing her and murdering Buckingham","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:46:55-07:00","id":1107077,"title":"","content":"Why now? Why not six months ago?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T12:36:14-07:00","id":1107090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=808965#post808965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Faster Travel is something that is problematic. Charms can help solve this, as does being a Sorcerer. I can't think of any other way.<br /> <br /> Better communication is iffy as hell. There is already &quot;God Prayer relay&quot; system mentioned in 1e Cult of the Illuminated, which I actually enjoyed. Sorcerous magical mirrors or that one skull talking necromancy spell helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>For faster Travel Breeding a Horse with a yeddim/eagle would be pretty good.<br /> <br /> For Better Communication since creation is flat something like the <a href=\"http://discworld.wikia.com/wiki/Clacks\" target=\"_blank\">Clacks</a> might work. Get some Demons or elementals to run it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T17:32:01-07:00","id":1107158,"title":"","content":"Normally I'd create a tower of Essence gathering machines and plug everybody inside in individual pods. And then I get a machine spirit to craft the best possible VR life for each of them so its absolutely the best quality of life they'll ever have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13507-nicklance","name":"NickLance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T17:51:31-07:00","id":1107161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NickLance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107158#post1107158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get a machine spirit to craft the best possible VR life for each of them</div> </div> </div> </div>Who makes that judgement?<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: This may actually prevent me from being able to sleep for a while, Jesus Christ...<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, if it was just the basic details, I would have... at the very least, questions about the viability. But that detail about how everybody is in an <i>individual</i> pod... the idea of every single human being existing in total isolation from every other...<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, even if I was to grant that it was possible to effectively simulate the complexities of numerous personalities and the interactions that arise therein, which I do not, just the notion, the idea of being robbed of the infinite nuances that arise from interactions with the unexpected, with the contrary, the ways in which the work of people who will never meet you or know your name can enrich your life...<br /> <br /> \u200bThe things that this premise would destroy... it's one of the most horrifying ideas I've ever come across. Utterly bone chilling. Having said my piece, I'm going to do my utmost to forget that I ever read it (largely through immersing myself in the work products of innumerable other actual living people).<br /> <br /> \u200bYeah, this was worth reviving an 18-month long dead topic for...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-23-2017, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T19:15:32-07:00","id":1107181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107161#post1107161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who makes that judgement?<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: This may actually prevent me from being able to sleep for a while, Jesus Christ...<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, if it was just the basic details, I would have... at the very least, questions about the viability. But that detail about how everybody is in an <i>individual</i> pod... the idea of every single human being existing in total isolation from every other...<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, even if I was to grant that it was possible to effectively simulate the complexities of numerous personalities and the interactions that arise therein, which I do not, just the notion, the idea of being robbed of the infinite nuances that arise from interactions with the unexpected, with the contrary, the ways in which the work of people who will never meet you or know your name can enrich your life...<br /> <br /> \u200bThe things that this premise would destroy... it's one of the most horrifying ideas I've ever come across. Utterly bone chilling. Having said my piece, I'm going to do my utmost to forget that I ever read it (largely through immersing myself in the work products of innumerable other actual living people).<br /> <br /> \u200bYeah, this was worth reviving an 18-month long dead topic for...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or effectively create The Matrix and let everyone live in a virtual world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13507-nicklance","name":"NickLance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T20:17:15-07:00","id":1107193,"title":"","content":"Hmm.... what about creating a race of servant golems? <br /> <br /> I mean, you can do it so that they are immortal, have the intelligence of a small child, and are basically automatons. They can learn things, and reproduce quickly. <br /> <br /> Ta-dah! Free labour! Have them work in the fields/ mines/ dangerous and boring work so that no one has to do it, and then your standard of living has increased!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T23:33:22-07:00","id":1107231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution#post808930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I have an idea of a Twilight Crafter that wants to improve the living conditions of Creation for mortals. Any ideas how I can do that without recreating the Industrial Revolution or the Ex2 First Age?<br /> <br /> Here are some areas of improvement areas I thought of:<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> One idea I had was focusing on the community instead of the individual. For example, instead of everyone having a phone, you go to the phone office or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar Twilight can learn the 2E enlightening charm to bring back the cultured Dragon Kings and have them live among mortals again. Time of Glory is not considered First Age right?<br /> <br /> Clean water: Read up on industrial lainas from the Scroll of Fallen Race, pg. 22, indoor plumbing, sewerage treatment, etc. with livinig vines that transplant water that also filters at the same time.<br /> Abundant Food: Growing Wood Path 2-3<br /> Climate Control: Pg. 22, Crystal Lights and Heaters<br /> Health Care: Yielding Earth Path 3-5, and Alchemical Shurbs in Pg. 22 again.<br /> Safe Lighting Crystal Lights and Heaters<br /> Faster Travels: Pg. 17, the Dragon King Tube Car transport system, also their lift tube system, and the main<br /> Better Communication: Pterok flying delivery services.<br /> More Accessible Education: That's what they did in the Time of Glories.<br /> Better Safety/Law Enforcement: Clear Air Path 5 is very useful for crime investigations.<br /> <br /> The Time of Glory is like the Garden of Eden. But without Solar social-fu, can you entice enough mortals to return to such Utopia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1561-kanchou","name":"Kanchou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T00:01:23-07:00","id":1107237,"title":"","content":"I love that someone necroed this post because the ideas presented here will be a gold mine for my character. <br /> <br /> That said I've come to understand that the absence of an easy life for mortals of creation has less to do with an absence of currently existing resources as much as it has to do with a disproportionate distribution of those resources based on a kind of magically powered class system.<br /> <br /> For this reason one of the things that my twilight is using to try to fix the situation long game is to promote a series of teaching that contain within them an ideology on how one should live their life.<br /> He is doing this using one of the lore custom Lore charms from the miricles of the exalted book as well as other lore charms, and the end goal is to promote this as the dominate ideology for all beings in creation, including spirits, exalted, and other non human mortals, to create a kind of group consciousness that will result in magically power luxury socialism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T00:09:29-07:00","id":1107242,"title":"","content":"..... one of the ideas i had to improve the standard of living was not to make better environments for mortals, but make mortals better. <br /> <br /> Don't want diseases? Give mortals resistance 5. Want tech? Intelligence 5, and merits to get perfect memories and shorter training times. So on and so forth. Make them better, stronger, faster, smarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T03:15:30-07:00","id":1107270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NickLance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107181#post1107181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or effectively create The Matrix and let everyone live in a virtual world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did we see the same movie? Wasn't one of the big points of <i>The Matrix</i> that it was a giant green shithole?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T04:05:05-07:00","id":1107280,"title":"","content":"Kind of... and at the same time, kind of not. That's what Cypher argued. Though in later films that discussion kind of disappeared (as did all other nuance and discussion).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T04:11:57-07:00","id":1107281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107270#post1107270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we see the same movie? Wasn't one of the big points of <i>The Matrix</i> that it was a giant green shithole?</div> </div> </div> </div>The argument that &quot;ignorance is bliss&quot; quite applies.<br /> <br /> But then again I tend to see Creation as a degree less crap-sack than the 40K universe, hence its better if people just become living batteries living in a virtual mmorpg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13507-nicklance","name":"NickLance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T04:35:16-07:00","id":1107284,"title":"","content":"Eh, I don't think Creation is that bad. Most people are just, you know, farmers or hunter-gatherers with a pretty normal standard of living for the 1st century AD. Sure, very occasionally fair folk might attack and eat everyone's emotions, or a demon might randomly appear and kill everyone, but that's not very likely, frankly. And of course, there's some magic that might defend against this stuff. So it ends up about the same.<br /> I mean, the 1st century AD was pretty rubbish, but it'd seem much easier to improve people's real lives than build them fake ones (since they've still got to be supplied with food and water and so on... huh, how do people reproduce when their minds are dreaming of a virtual world?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T05:03:37-07:00","id":1107286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NickLance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107281#post1107281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The argument that &quot;ignorance is bliss&quot; quite applies.</div> </div> </div> </div>So mind-raping their memories away or raising them from birth so that your fake world is the only one they know <i>is better?</i> <br /> <br /> I mean, seriously, people in <i>The Truman Show</i> objected to Christof's whole setup for Truman for a reason, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107284#post1107284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">huh, how do people reproduce when their minds are dreaming of a virtual world?).</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't, remember? They were grown in &quot;fields, endless fields.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-24-2017, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T05:55:16-07:00","id":1107290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NickLance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107281#post1107281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The argument that &quot;ignorance is bliss&quot; quite applies.<br /> <br /> But then again I tend to see Creation as a degree less crap-sack than the 40K universe, hence its better if people just become living batteries living in a virtual mmorpg.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is hilarious, because on the whole, the 40K galaxy <i>isn't that bad</i>.<br /> <br /> Canonically, most planets in the Imperium are &quot;Civilized Worlds&quot;, where the inhabitants enjoy technology, civil liberties and other amenities that someone from the 21st century would recognize and appreciate. The Imperium has official-and-recognized diplomatic relations with the Eldar Craftwords and the Tau Septs, the concept of religious freedom (as long as you worship the God-Emperor, the Ecclesiarchy doesn't really care <u>how</u>), and even on Hive Worlds, life isn't <u>all shitdark, all the time.</u><br /> <br /> Read some of the novels sometime. Not every planet is Cadia or Armageddon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T07:47:10-07:00","id":1107311,"title":"","content":"Well, actually you don't have to worship the God-Emperor if you're a Techpriest. Or a forge-world menial. Although most ministorum priests would probably claim that it's okay because Tech-Priests worship the Emperor in their own way, they just call him the Omnissiah (because it's much easier to claim that than have the lights in your cathedral stop working).<br /> <br /> I'm running Rogue Trader at the moment, and the Missionary and Explorator are constantly clashing over religion, and trying to gain influence in all of the non-Imperials they have to draft to maintain their ship's population.<br /> <br /> I think &quot;enjoy civil liberties that someone from the 21st century would appreciate&quot; is perhaps a bit of an optimistic view of the average Imperial world though. I imagine the average Imperial World to be something like the PRC: it's not like everyone's in constant fear at all times, and people grumble about local governors, but if you start talking about how the system is bad, or the top levels of government, it's unlikely to go well for you. And you don't have to follow the exact form of religion mandated, there's a few alternatives, but you're likely to have problems, and there's a lot of religious movements that are punishable by imprisonment (or death).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-24-2017, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T10:07:32-07:00","id":1107349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107311#post1107311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, actually you don't have to worship the God-Emperor if you're a Techpriest. Or a forge-world menial. Although most ministorum priests would probably claim that it's okay because Tech-Priests worship the Emperor in their own way, they just call him the Omnissiah (because it's much easier to claim that than have the lights in your cathedral stop working).<br /> <br /> I'm running Rogue Trader at the moment, and the Missionary and Explorator are constantly clashing over religion, and trying to gain influence in all of the non-Imperials they have to draft to maintain their ship's population.<br /> <br /> I think &quot;enjoy civil liberties that someone from the 21st century would appreciate&quot; is perhaps a bit of an optimistic view of the average Imperial world though. I imagine the average Imperial World to be something like the PRC: it's not like everyone's in constant fear at all times, and people grumble about local governors, but if you start talking about how the system is bad, or the top levels of government, it's unlikely to go well for you. And you don't have to follow the exact form of religion mandated, there's a few alternatives, but you're likely to have problems, and there's a lot of religious movements that are punishable by imprisonment (or death).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Read some of the Black Library novels, especially the ones by Dan Abnett. He makes life, even on a horribly-polluted Hive World, sound ...... relatively ok, if not nice. I didn't recoil in horror when reading about Vervunhive, at least not until it got attacked by Chaos.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T10:22:14-07:00","id":1107359,"title":"","content":"Well, sure. I lived for 4 years in a dictatorship, and it's not really that bad. I'm always interested when I meet students talking about their lives in various countries with poor human rights records, brutal dictators, and so on, and... they don't sound that bad. Because for most people, it's not. Like, a Syrian student of mine from Homs was talking about his life before the war, playing football, having house parties, going to Church, playing the drums, etc. It sounded fine. But that didn't mean he had much in the way of civil liberties, because the Ba'athist regime was a police state.<br /> But the main thing I've found, visiting various dicatorships, is how normal life seems (I mean, it's not like I could see all the Falun Gong members in the local prison). It's just occasionally that you get screwed by it. Mostly, it's just a kind of constant annoyance because of the way you have to self-censor.<br /> <br /> My point is, for most people in the Imperium, life's okay. The main problems they have are stuff like how working in a factory is pretty dull, or how the government spends quite a high portion of GDP on defence so taxes are high for the services you get. But it's misleading to say that most of them have civil liberties that we would appreciate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T12:21:52-07:00","id":1107398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NickLance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107181#post1107181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Or effectively create The Matrix and let everyone live in a virtual world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively this can be seen as an excellent example of how a demon or Rakasha with their alien ways of thinking might try to &quot;help&quot; humanity if they were of a mind to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T15:48:03-07:00","id":1107432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107193#post1107193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.... what about creating a race of servant golems? <br /> <br /> I mean, you can do it so that they are immortal, have the intelligence of a small child, and are basically automatons. They can learn things, and reproduce quickly. <br /> <br /> Ta-dah! Free labour! Have them work in the fields/ mines/ dangerous and boring work so that no one has to do it, and then your standard of living has increased!</div> </div> </div> </div>And you've wrecked your economy. What are you planning to do with all the people your golems just put out of work? Sure, you can start retraining everyone, but you said the golems can learn and reproduce, so your new slave caste might well end up taking lots more jobs than you expected over time.<br /> <br /> Or rise up in revolt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T15:53:15-07:00","id":1107434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107398#post1107398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively this can be seen as an excellent example of how a demon or Rakasha with their alien ways of thinking might try to &amp;quot;help&amp;quot; humanity if they were of a mind to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I built a Raksha once who was very dedicated to the role of the Kind Princess. She saw the plight of the humans in Creation, always having to work hard instead of just willing things into existence on a whim. Thus, she and her servants, went forth to engage in complex geomantic engineering to infect Creation with the Wyld and turn it into one big archipelago of middlemarch areas on the shores of the deep Wyld.<br /> <br /> She expects that everyone will really appreciate it when she's finished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T20:15:13-07:00","id":1107497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107432#post1107432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you've wrecked your economy. What are you planning to do with all the people your golems just put out of work? Sure, you can start retraining everyone, but you said the golems can learn and reproduce, so your new slave caste might well end up taking lots more jobs than you expected over time.<br /> <br /> Or rise up in revolt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno?<br /> <br /> Nothing?<br /> <br /> What i mean is, instead of having machines to do everyhing for you, get the slave caste to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T00:57:53-07:00","id":1107567,"title":"","content":"Getting an eclipse to establish firmly binding trade and nonaggression treaties over an entire region, or a zenith founding a religion of peace that the ruling bodies actually adhere to could also help. Without wars (or at least a lot fewer), there will be more able bodied workers available for food and tool production, less damage will be done to crops and buildings and fewer sick and crippled people will rely on support from others. And that's on top of the benefit of having fewer families be torn apart, which I'd say also improves the standard of liiving overall.<br /> <br /> Maintaining this peace would be an effort, at least at first, but with sufficient magic should be able to became lasting. This would be a high profile endeavour, however, and so might draw wyld hunt attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T01:27:48-07:00","id":1107574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107432#post1107432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you've wrecked your economy. What are you planning to do with all the people your golems just put out of work? Sure, you can start retraining everyone, but you said the golems can learn and reproduce, so your new slave caste might well end up taking lots more jobs than you expected over time.<br /> <br /> Or rise up in revolt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> can't wreck an economy if you abolish currency and create an equal distribution of resources","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T01:42:35-07:00","id":1107579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107432#post1107432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you've wrecked your economy. What are you planning to do with all the people your golems just put out of work? Sure, you can start retraining everyone, but you said the golems can learn and reproduce, so your new slave caste might well end up taking lots more jobs than you expected over time.<br /> <br /> Or rise up in revolt.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the short term, it's a problem. In the long term, people move into higher-skilled jobs and the economy improves. Though you do need to educate them.<br /> But then, now you've got the golems to do manual labour, you've got the time and resources to educate people.<br /> But honestly, farmers are not going to complain about being given 2 or 3 golems to come and work on their farm and do the hard stuff, are they?<br /> <br /> I mean, industrialisation has led to a better economy in the real world, overall.<br /> <br /> Saying this, you are somewhat right; it does have to be handled with care. You can do it the right way (here's 2 golems to help on your farm) or the wrong way (that farm is now run by golems, so you, Mr+Mrs Farmer, can leave and go... I dunno, wherever). You would need to think it through in order to not fill your cities with beggars. But it's a viable idea (and, as ideas on this thread go, not that impractical. Certainly a lot easier than the putting-people-in-dream-pods idea).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-25-2017, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T03:07:01-07:00","id":1107591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107574#post1107574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can't wreck an economy if you abolish currency and create an equal distribution of resources</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense that you can't kill a man after already having killed him, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T06:47:46-07:00","id":1107616,"title":"","content":"This post is addressing the drift on society planning, just to clear.<br /> <br /> So a key thing to remember when planning large scale societies is this:<br /> <br /> <b>You *are* going to kill and/or displace innocent people. Period. No matter how powerful you are. No matter how wise you are. No matter how strong you are. Why?</b><br /> <br /> You see, some humans have this emotional attachment to their ways of life. They don't want to hurt anyone, and they don't want to stand in the way of progress, but, you can't tell them what to do. So what do you do with them? Disenfranchise them? Yeah, real enlightened. Gotta break a few eggs right? No no it's OK I'm different because I'm a Twilight!<br /> <br /> Look, people do not follow long-term incentives blindly, and in some cases, even short term incentives with mountains of evidence in favor of them. I mean, just look around at our own world. Let me put it in game-speak: You're really gonna erode multiple level 3 intimacies to replace them with your own, in likely at least thousands of people in a city-state sized area, and you're the good guys? The march of progress? I can see why some people might not see it that way. So what do you do about them? What happens if some of these people are your key society members?<br /> <br /> In short, it sounds like a fantastic game of Exalted to *try* to improve the standard of living through large scale society change, but not necessarily to succeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T08:36:46-07:00","id":1107644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107591#post1107591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the sense that you can't kill a man after already having killed him, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially yes, the argument being made is that the golems will destroy people's livelihoods by replacing their jobs and making them destitute, and if you abolished capitalism and removed the fear of death as the incentive to work then. It only would you improve people's lives by removing that obsticle, but by having golems take over all hard labor you would free the population up to pursue their own interests of study.<br /> <br /> Of course <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar255_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"255\" data-vbnamecard=\"255\">ParanoiaCombo</a> is correct in asserting that this is only going to make you the good guy to some people and to other they will hate you, for example someone like trump would hate you for making people's lives easier just like someone who's family had worked their farm for countless generations might hate you as well.<br /> One of those two types is evil and as an exalted one of your jobs is to vanquish evil if you feel like it, but the case of the farmer who just wants to stay a farmer presents greater difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T10:54:55-07:00","id":1107683,"title":"","content":"The problem with any system such as that is that it still needs to deal with the issue of resources and work product being limited, and the matter of how to organise distribution of them.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven if one posits a highly idealised system in which no necessary materials are scarce, there will always be even just momentary limits in the existence of certain things owing to the time that it takes to create them.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust coming up with a system of distribution that people would widely accept would be difficult enough, but if it was centrally organised it runs into the issue that all attempts to centrally organise control of incredibly complex social systems do; the sheer scope of the task makes it extremely difficult to formulate policies that can effectively manage it, and the number of moving parts (i.e. staff) inherent to trying to implement such systems create so many points of failure.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne of the benefits of having a medium of exchange and systemized valuation is that it allows the work of ensuring that people acquire necessary or desired resources is widely distributed and can have responsibility taken for it in small packages. What do you do when the weekly food allowances of tens of thousands of people go awry because the paperwork was misfiled?<br /> <br /> \u200bCapitalism has a lot of issues when it comes to concentration of buying power in the hands of a small number of elites, or facilitating systems for the exploitation of large groups, but it also has so much of a basis in increasing innovation and overall prosperity that I don't think it should be written off entirely. Something like communism has the fundamental problem that it is basically chasing a fairy tale, a system that relies on so many idealised details that it's only of use to perfectly spherical cows, and, personally, I think I would not like it so much even if there was some silver bullet that allowed it to function harmoniously.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T11:44:25-07:00","id":1107696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107683#post1107683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with any system such as that is that it still needs to deal with the issue of resources and work product being limited, and the matter of how to organise distribution of them.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven if one posits a highly idealised system in which no necessary materials are scarce, there will always be even just momentary limits in the existence of certain things owing to the time that it takes to create them.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust coming up with a system of distribution that people would widely accept would be difficult enough, but if it was centrally organised it runs into the issue that all attempts to centrally organise control of incredibly complex social systems do; the sheer scope of the task makes it extremely difficult to formulate policies that can effectively manage it, and the number of moving parts (i.e. staff) inherent to trying to implement such systems create so many points of failure.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne of the benefits of having a medium of exchange and systemized valuation is that it allows the work of ensuring that people acquire necessary or desired resources is widely distributed and can have responsibility taken for it in small packages. What do you do when the weekly food allowances of tens of thousands of people go awry because the paperwork was misfiled?<br /> <br /> \u200bCapitalism has a lot of issues when it comes to concentration of buying power in the hands of a small number of elites, or facilitating systems for the exploitation of large groups, but it also has so much of a basis in increasing innovation and overall prosperity that I don't think it should be written off entirely. Something like communism has the fundamental problem that it is basically chasing a fairy tale, a system that relies on so many idealised details that it's only of use to perfectly spherical cows, and, personally, I think I would not like it so much even if there was some silver bullet that allowed it to function harmoniously.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's quite a bit of an oversimplification I think given the assumption that human beings are inherantly geared to fail unless overseen by systems of capitalism, and it ignores the fact that capitalism is in itself an equally complex system, with the only difference being that it is already in practice.<br /> <br /> The difference between capitalism and socialism however, and by this I mean actual socialism not the brands of socialism that we've seen that are one step away from capitalism, is that in the system of capitalism people are rewarded for braking the system in this way and causing inequality because in capitalism, at a fundamental leve, for a person to succeed in attaining anything other than an modest scale, is the disenfranchisement of others.<br /> <br /> All of the benefits that people in the global north enjoy is due primarily to the fact that we use underpaid or forced labor in much of the third world while underpaying countries for their valuable resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/amp/grist.org/business-technology/none-of-the-worlds-top-industries-would-be-profitable-if-they-paid-for-the-natural-capital-they-use/amp/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/amp/grist.org/business-technology/none-of-the-worlds-top-industries-would-be-profitable-if-they-paid-for-the-natural-capital-they-use/amp/\" target=\"_blank\"> Redirect Notice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/amp/grist.org/business-technology/none-of-the-worlds-top-industries-would-be-profitable-if-they-paid-for-the-natural-capital-they-use/amp/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.google.com/amp/grist.org/business-technology/none-of-the-worlds-top-industries-would-be-profitable-if-they-paid-for-the-natural-capital-they-use/amp/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.exposingtruth.com/new-un-report-finds-almost-no-industry-profitable-if-environmental-costs-were-included/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.exposingtruth.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/pollution2.jpg?fit=800%2C533&amp;ssl=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.exposingtruth.com/new-un-report-finds-almost-no-industry-profitable-if-environmental-costs-were-included/\" target=\"_blank\"> New UN report finds almost no industry profitable if environmental costs were included </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.exposingtruth.com/new-un-report-finds-almost-no-industry-profitable-if-environmental-costs-were-included/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.exposingtruth.com/new-un-report-finds-almost-no-industry-profitable-if-environmental-costs-were-included/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> If you haven&rsquo;t been paying attention, I don&rsquo;t blame you for at first not believing this. After all, companies go to great lengths to greenwash their image and present themselves as prog&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here are two articles that detail how industies, if they were forced to pay for the ecological side effects of their industies would be unprofitable, and this doesn't even cover the under paid workers and the like.<br /> <br /> Alternatively think of an example of fully automated luxury socialism that we have. Tbf it is entirely fictional, but Star Trek.<br /> <br /> This is a setting where money has been abolished on an interplanetary level and the resources are shared by all people's, helped primarily by an ability to manufacture resources through the existence of replicators, which is a process not too difficult to recreate in creation using some charms. <br /> <br /> Is there opportunity for corruption or misfilings, yes definitely, just as there are in all systems, but we have a giant buracracy stat for a reason, and at the least this system is not inherantly geared towards causing some suffering for the benefit of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T12:53:54-07:00","id":1107719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107696#post1107696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's quite a bit of an oversimplification I think given the assumption that human beings are inherantly geared to fail unless overseen by systems of capitalism, and it ignores the fact that capitalism is in itself an equally complex system, with the only difference being that it is already in practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNo, the difference is that it is not centrally controlled.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich I outlined in the very post that you're quoting.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I do appreciate the irony in somebody contesting the assertion that central planning of civilization would not work because civilization is too complicated by stating that the assertion is a simplification)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the benefits that people in the global north enjoy is due primarily to the fact that we use underpaid or forced labor in much of the third world while underpaying countries for their valuable resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm reminded of how Henry Ford famously recognised that the best way for him to actually make money was to pay his own workers a decent wage so that they would be able to actually buy the cars they built.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich is to say, I think the logic that says that prosperity is wholly dependent on the exploitation of somebody is based on observations that are understandable, but have faults.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt also reminds me about how I have read studies observing that things such as benefits and a good work environment actually make businesses more productive, because happy, motivated workers make better use of their time.<br /> <br /> The narrative that an inequitable system is an optimised one has a number of holes in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/amp/grist.org/business-technology/none-of-the-worlds-top-industries-would-be-profitable-if-they-paid-for-the-natural-capital-they-use/amp/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/amp/grist.org/business-technology/none-of-the-worlds-top-industries-would-be-profitable-if-they-paid-for-the-natural-capital-they-use/amp/\" target=\"_blank\"> Redirect Notice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/amp/grist.org/business-technology/none-of-the-worlds-top-industries-would-be-profitable-if-they-paid-for-the-natural-capital-they-use/amp/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.google.com/amp/grist.org/business-technology/none-of-the-worlds-top-industries-would-be-profitable-if-they-paid-for-the-natural-capital-they-use/amp/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.exposingtruth.com/new-un-report-finds-almost-no-industry-profitable-if-environmental-costs-were-included/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.exposingtruth.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/pollution2.jpg?fit=800%2C533&amp;ssl=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.exposingtruth.com/new-un-report-finds-almost-no-industry-profitable-if-environmental-costs-were-included/\" target=\"_blank\"> New UN report finds almost no industry profitable if environmental costs were included </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.exposingtruth.com/new-un-report-finds-almost-no-industry-profitable-if-environmental-costs-were-included/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.exposingtruth.com/new-un-report-finds-almost-no-industry-profitable-if-environmental-costs-were-included/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> If you haven&rsquo;t been paying attention, I don&rsquo;t blame you for at first not believing this. After all, companies go to great lengths to greenwash their image and present themselves as prog&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here are two articles that detail how industies, if they were forced to pay for the ecological side effects of their industies would be unprofitable, and this doesn't even cover the under paid workers and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'll look at them later, but I'll admit that the outline that you've stated has me suspicious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a setting where money has been abolished on an interplanetary level and the resources are shared by all peoples</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Star Trek, and some of its merits have their ideals, but it's a subject that breaks down in several areas if one tries to examine it thoroughly. For example, Jean-Luc Picard's family owns a vineyard that produces wine; how does that work?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">helped primarily by an ability to manufacture resources through the existence of replicators</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's another key area; replicators are themselves a limited resource, as is the energy required to power them. This is a cornerstone of many Star Trek plots.<br /> <br /> \u200bNote that the limit on replicators is not only a matter of their number, but their productivity. At what rate can replicators produce materials? How much material is required at any given time? Even in the best circumstances, there is going to be a waiting list; how is it organised?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there opportunity for corruption or misfilings, yes definitely, just as there are in all systems</div> </div> </div> </div>But the distribution of those inefficiencies is not random; it correlates to the complexity of the system. The more complex the system, the more it compounds failures.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat goes for any system, whether it be a mechanism, an organisation, or a living organism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">we have a giant buracracy stat for a reason</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYes, but I don't think that it's the reason that you think it is.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's partially a matter of how I'm averse to the idea that any result that a player/character desires can be achieved if one rolls sufficient successes, regardless of their plausibility, and partially a matter of simple volume.<br /> <br /> \u200bHow many problems can a Solar handle at once? I assert that it would be fewer than the Solar would be faced with if they tried to create a system to try and centrally govern every aspect of life.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy main interest in this is not with the idea that power gives one a means to flatten out all of the complexities of a diverse world filled with many distinct and often contradictory groups and trends and agendas, but leaves them well equipped to come up with effective compromises (or creates interesting scenarios out of the refusal to compromise).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T13:34:34-07:00","id":1107742,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest guys, it seems a little odd to say that the way to sort out people's living standards in Creation is that you need to get rid of capitalism.<br /> <br /> It's a pre-modern setting. Most people do not live in capitalist economies. (They also do not live in command economies)<br /> <br /> Most people live in feudal economies, or as hunter-gatherers, or in very simple pre-capitalist economies, or in small scale cooperatives, or in some mix thereof. In fact, some of them live in what could be argued to be small-scale socialist economies, village communes where everyone works together for mutual benefit.<br /> <br /> So there's no point saying &quot;The answer is to destroy capitalism! Put the factories under worker control and destroy the capitalist class of owners of the means of production!&quot; Because most means of production are either owned by private artisans, guilds, or the government anyway (who don't use the workers as wage-slaves to exploit said means of production; they don't let it be exploited at all, because the King wants to hunt in that forest, not let filthy peasants cut down trees to make stuff out of).<br /> I guess it is reasonable to say that people in the rich countries (ie the Realm) should stop exploiting the poorer countries (the Threshold), but that's done through direct taxation, not complex unfair trading systems.<br /> <br /> There are probably political/economic changes that need to be made, but in most societies, there aren't that many goods to redistribute; the key thing is making sure the peasants actually produce enough goods in the first place to not starve! And not tax them 40% to build your castle and have fancy noble parties and stuff, of course.<br /> You don't want to be like Stalin, trying to redistribute the food produced by the peasants, except it turns out there's not actually enough food for everyone anyway so the peasants starve to death because you took their grain, and then grain production falls further.<br /> <br /> I mean, when we had the Peasants' Revolt in the 14th century, they weren't demanding the abolition of money, redistribution of capital, the nationalisation of industry, etc. They weren't trying to abolish capitalism, because they didn't have it; they were trying to abolish serfdom, because that's what they had. Also, reduced taxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-25-2017, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T14:20:23-07:00","id":1107762,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we got a bit off track there, didn't we?<br /> <br /> \u200bPointing out certain systems of pre-modern economics does bring me to one point regarding the idea that the existence of working automatons would necessarily improve standards of living, though, because it feels very reminiscent of my favourite old standby of &quot;Roman slave labour created massive numbers of unemployed people who contributed to the social instability that destroyed the Roman Republic&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust as an example of something rather similar that created problems in the long run. And that was even a system where the government actually provided a grain dole and the culture had the notion of things like a patronage system in which being unemployed didn't necessarily mean you struggled financially.<br /> <br /> \u200bA major problem there was that large numbers of people who were otherwise unoccupied had a tendency to become frustrated and unstimulated enough to form gangs, being financially beholden to elites often made them function as private armies with which the elites could play out their political disputes by prompting the groups to brawl with one another, and the need to maintain a constant grain supply at the expense of the state prompted a lot of the famous Roman foreign policy.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe point about peasants also brings up a notion about different priorities for different people; I would find it credible that the majority of farmers in Creation don't want to not have to work, they just want to be able to keep and sell more of what their work produces, have that work not be made too hard by deleterious weather conditions, and be allowed to buy whatever they can afford as a result of selling their produce. Their context informs their worldview, and their worldview informs their momentary wants. That and certain cultural ideas, such as maybe a desire to personally engage in the work that their own kin did for the sake of maintaining a lifestyle continuity.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat and, when farming conditions are good, the number of hours you work aren't very long, and when economic conditions are favourable you can spend the free time engaged in various kinds of festivities, as was the norm following the Black Plague.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I'm starting to ramble...<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm also worried that I'm just repeating things that I've already said in this thread, because I can't remember, <i>because the last time I posted things in this thread was a <b>year and a half ago</b></i>, so I don't quite feel stimulated.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T14:53:34-07:00","id":1107766,"title":"","content":"Excellent post, Wizard. The problems these people in Creation face (if it's anything like our world), and that those among the Solar Exalted who seek progress immediately have to contend with are (non-exhaustively!) the problems of banditry, despotism, lacks of individual rights, fair judiciary and law enforcement, natural disasters, disease and really, as you say, very low levels of general <b>productivity</b> (in agriculture, manufacturing, services), of resource use and of education.<br /> <br /> The questions of Capitalism are (briefly) of the justice in an economic system where you are actually achieving much higher productivity, but through workers who are reliant on using capital goods owned by others. Those questions which are of the just (or at least utility maximizing) distribution of that profit and ownership of those capital goods are <i>far </i>off in their future (if Creation is such that they ever become relevant on mass scale!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T18:05:34-07:00","id":1107830,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107742#post1107742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest guys, it seems a little odd to say that the way to sort out people's living standards in Creation is that you need to get rid of capitalism.<br /> <br /> It's a pre-modern setting. Most people do not live in capitalist economies. (They also do not live in command economies)<br /> <br /> Most people live in feudal economies, or as hunter-gatherers, or in very simple pre-capitalist economies, or in small scale cooperatives, or in some mix thereof. In fact, some of them live in what could be argued to be small-scale socialist economies, village communes where everyone works together for mutual benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>now this is very interesting, although my comments above had as much to do for why socialism is a source of whoa in our own world, i love that once again i am reminded that the setting would not function under the same rules as our own reality given that it's not a modern setting, it helps me better conceptualize the setting and i actually love the portrait you painted here in your description.<br /> <br /> I think one of my points of confusion though is where the guild comes in, because although yes i grasp that most of creation acts as higherarchal areas of rule, espeacially those areas controlled by or connected to the realm, the books themselves seem to describe the guild as an equally powerful force, so how does that play in?<br /> <br /> also the absence of abusive capitalism doesn't change the sentiment so much as now it is just an abusive monarchal or feudal system, the concept of liberating the masses remains the same imo on how one can benefit all beings in creation, it just about thinking along the right terms, which you have helped me do already.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":1990,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","user":"norraba","date":". 06-26-2017, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T18:57:58-07:00","id":1107846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1107762#post1107762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Roman slave labour created massive numbers of unemployed people who contributed to the social instability that destroyed the Roman Republic&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall a rather interesting discussion that it also stifled innovation. Since (slave) labor was so cheap, there was no profit motive to invest in labor saving devices. In fact, I seem to recall that it was your own post months+ ago involving how after the black death in England workers were so well paid they could spend half the year on festivals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T14:10:25-07:00","id":1108508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=808957#post808957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can dig wells for people. Maybe introduce irrigation canals or help them improve their farming.<br /> <br /> Seriously, playing a Twilight <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norman_Borlaug\" target=\"_blank\">Norman Borlaug</a> would be awesome IMO.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This too. Introducing ideas such as &quot;Hey, what if we DON'T just throw our shit into the streets?&quot; and &quot;Maybe we should wash our hands once a day&quot; could be <b>massive</b>. Like how <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ignaz_Semmelweis\" target=\"_blank\">Ignaz Semmelweis</a> noticed that if you washed and disinfected your hands before a surgery, the patient's chances of survival increased drastically. Just small ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're coming off as a bit more arrogant than you intend to. The idea of washing yourself so that that way you can prevent sores or you don't taste Minore isn't exactly some radical idea two civilized people. Even with a Bronze Age lifestyle. Even in a tribal lifestyle. The matter is making it convenient easy and pleasant in order to do so. In particular where are they going to get the water and soap in order to scrub themselves up with. And how will they do so as part of their lifestyle and work schedule. Technology matters yes but all too often it's nearly a leaver to social revolutions not the utter and complete cause. Before the Gutenberg printing press there existed a technology that allowed for Mass printing that became actually more prominent in producing more literary material.<br /> the printing press was as much a physical invention as it was a sign of a revolution in terms of thought information needed to be more prominent and distributed. Or at least this was the understanding of what got attached to it.<br /> so yes health and sanitation great crops rotation as well as farming techniques food distribution and preservation methods all of these things very much matter. Some of the great Super Heroes of Greek mythology often make the simplest things that we take for granted Daedalus he of the labyrinth Builder and making the wings of wax and all of that stuff? Yet his big real super invention that changed the world and made him rival to Festus himself was the saw. Sometimes the simplest most easily to proliferate invention matters more than all the grand works in the world. Just figuring out for instance a means to make and hold together brick as well as a basic easy to duplicate and modify design and a teaching school for saying architecture will be revolutionary to a great deal of the threshold civilizations. Heck even some of the ones in the Blessed Isle if this information was something that they could pick up and replicate with tools and materials that they had it at hand.<br /> <br /> this is probably for the best after all more complex Works will alternator and the surrounding area which means that you'll be a hit up by the local protection racket in the form of the Gods and the Elementals. The hilarious part this means that chances are while you'll still be hunted down by the wild Hunt they'll be unable to remove your works as readily as if you build a castle to your own ego. One of the female admirals from the aspect books found out that she had to kill every single member of a tried because they had for the most part been trained and brainwashed by a rogue solar, Leda.<br /> <br /> So first you want to think what's the Baseline that everybody is living their day-to-day lives in how do they eat how do they sleep what do they drink and why do they do at how do their families live and what can you provide them that would change their lifestyle to be for the better but also fit within their cultural context enough so the thinking accepted even if the changes start to pile on. Public bass for instance might be one thing. But what if you literally were able to make a type of tub that were able to fit in everybody's home but was easy to use and easy to heat up and easy to clean. What if you made a form of soap or a formula for it that me that was good for cleaning the body and another that was good for cleaning your cookware as well as your house and or prevent buildup of infection and make the place smell nice. Yeah basic household goods. Nails standard rise nuts toilet paper. I know all of this seems ridiculous but sometimes you don't have to go big. What if you made a type of compost pit that was easier to use but managed to contain the smell and was able to more effectively create or make fertilizer out of the waste. And the cool thing because so much of exalted is Magic is that you can make a semi technological basis for this and yet Enchanted in order to work even better. The recycle of waste into healthier that then feeds wood or plant life should be something that's a basic understanding of thaumaturgical principles. So making a bunch of rather cheap artifacts or just the equivalent of not artifacts that sometimes get made such like Seven Devils powder or other things could actually be interesting. And short try not to build giant single mansa's for your entire Hearthstone try to build lots of little things that makes everyone's lives for convenient and better.<br /> I know this is crazy but some places in creation are waiting for revolutions like standardized folding chairs and tables tires bridles and harnesses. Or even Bellow pumps and beds. There's a lot about our modern-day life that we just sort of take for granted including such basic things as illumination. Good warm lighting could probably be relatively minor as it imitates the most basic aspect of your own aminah and yet be easy to reproduce and hopefully easy for someone else to fix repair and make Pleasant with.<br /> <br /> Moreover if you can make sure that you can focus on function as opposed to form you may be able to make variations based on every local culture tradition or God. And if you factor in the God's prayers are function there in that means believe it or not you can make it so every time someone takes a bath or cleans out their crap they're basically being honored. And yes there are actual real world gods that are associated with dung and bathing<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T23:06:37-07:00","id":1416801,"title":"","content":"*raises hands* <br /> <br /> I think I remember seeing some water pills that can easily clear up entire tanks of water. How about a plant that produces berries or leaves that swiftly and easily purify water if they are crushed and put inside tanks or barrels of water?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T23:49:32-07:00","id":1416806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1416801#post1416801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*raises hands* <br /> <br /> I think I remember seeing some water pills that can easily clear up entire tanks of water. How about a plant that produces berries or leaves that swiftly and easily purify water if they are crushed and put inside tanks or barrels of water?</div> </div> </div> </div>Water purification tablets are usually iodine (toxic, mildly radioactive) or chlorine (bleach, swimming pool water).<br /> <br /> Both are better than water with e. coli or thick with bacteria.<br /> <br /> But sure, the basic idea sound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T00:13:03-07:00","id":1416809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1416806#post1416806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Water purification tablets are usually iodine (toxic, mildly radioactive) or chlorine (bleach, swimming pool water).<br /> <br /> Both are better than water with e. coli or thick with bacteria.<br /> <br /> But sure, the basic idea sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrugs* To be honest, I'm actually thinking of a terrestrial 3 working of a plant that has anti-bacterial and anti-viral properties, and is then enhanced by the sorcerous working to work better (no antibiotic resistance, no toxicity to humans). <br /> <br /> Come to think of it, a whole lot of ideas can be created by having terrestrial workings on plants and then expanding it outwards. Maybe instead of magitech, we have lots and lots of biotech plants and animals and everything in between? Yeah sure, not many machines... but with plants and animals doing so much of the work, why bother? <br /> <br /> Maybe even make chickens that make one egg a day and are far easier to keep, with the eggs having super-nutritious properties. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T20:33:26-07:00","id":1417094,"title":"","content":"One way is to create the equivalent of power tools. Being a moderately competent woodworker, I know from direct experience how much faster and easier power tools make the relevant processes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T20:38:00-07:00","id":1417097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/808930-improving-the-standard-of-living-without-recreating-the-industrial-revolution?p=1417094#post1417094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way is to create the equivalent of power tools. Being a moderately competent woodworker, I know from direct experience how much faster and easier power tools make the relevant processes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Centralized power tools based on gears and pulleys, powered by a single demon or an animal bred for strength and stamina? <br /> <br /> Though that runs into issues with you know, industrialization","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T07:52:36-07:00","id":1417144,"title":"","content":"Then find a way to create something analogous to the Shopsmith Mark V or Mark VII, a single power source that the artisan connects to various tools. This allows both high productivity per person, which is the one most important element in determining living standards, and also allows the avoidance of industrialization as we commonly use that term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}